{"jobs":[{"absolute_url":"https://nuro.ai/careersitem?gh_jid=8227642","data_compliance":[{"type":"gdpr","requires_consent":false,"requires_processing_consent":false,"requires_retention_consent":false,"retention_period":null,"demographic_data_consent_applies":false}],"internal_job_id":3560730,"location":{"name":"Mountain View, California (HQ)"},"metadata":[{"id":53829309,"name":"Location","value":"California - HQ","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":4977510,"name":"Department","value":"Legal","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":954897,"name":"Job Family","value":"Employment Law","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":4993730,"name":"Time Type","value":"Full-time","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":4978502,"name":"Worker Sub-Type","value":"Regular","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":6653805,"name":"Department (Job Board)","value":"Legal","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":6644840,"name":"Org (Job Board)","value":"Public Trust","value_type":"single_select"}],"id":8227642,"updated_at":"2026-10-09T11:02:43-04:00","requisition_id":"R-103143","title":"Assistant General Counsel, Employment","company_name":"Nuro","first_published":"2026-09-23T18:38:33-04:00","language":"en","application_deadline":null,"content":"&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nuro believes self-driving vehicles are the most immediate and profound opportunity for AI to drive positive change in the physical world. Safer streets, more time for what matters, and easier access to the world around us, that’s why we’re building a universal autonomy platform: self-driving for all roads and all rides.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Founded in 2016, Nuro is a physical AI company developing Level 4 autonomous driving technology for a wide range of vehicles, use cases, and markets. Powered by the Nuro Driver™, our universal autonomy platform enables the global mobility ecosystem to deploy autonomy at scale, from robotaxis and logistics fleets to personal vehicles.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;With years of real-world deployment experience and a flexible, partner-led business model, Nuro is working toward a future where millions of autonomous vehicles powered by our technology help make everyday life safer, easier, and more connected.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Nuro has raised over $2B in capital from Uber, NVIDIA, Google, Softbank, Fidelity, T. Rowe Price, and other leading investors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Assistant General Counsel, Employment, you will provide pragmatic day-to-day employment law advice in order to unblock business needs, mitigate risk, and incorporate best employment compliance practices throughout the company. You’ll play a critical role in building and upholding Nuro’s culture and helping prepare Nuro for the challenges and opportunities of launching a commercial product. This role will report directly to the Chief Legal Officer and serve as a key partner to the People team and business leaders, providing the legal, strategic, and operational framework to support an expanding global workforce.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Work&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;As the head of Nuro’s employment law function, you will be the owner of the company’s employment practices, actively seeking out opportunities to add value and strengthen the day-to-day activities of our People and Operations teams. You will advise on best practices and risk mitigation for the entire employee life-cycle (from recruiting to separation).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will collaborate with cross-functional teams to ensure that our employment policies, practices and programs are legally sound and best in class. You will&amp;nbsp; and maintain employment templates, policies, and training.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ll also be the primary point of contact for any employment pre-litigation and litigation matters, including any agency charges (DLSE, EEOC, DOL, CDR, etc.), discovery, motion practice, witness preparation, settlement negotiations, and trial/arbitration strategies, and you will help supervise and direct outside counsel support as necessary.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will partner closely with the People and Operations team to assist in the scaling of Nuro’s non-exempt workforce, including wage and hour compliance, drug testing regulations, and terminations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will own the employment legal and operation strategy for international growth and mobility issues, including to the EU, Asia, and Canada.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will partner closely on internal investigations and employee relations matters, including processes and policies and recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will support and advise on a wide variety of cross-functional areas, including leaves of absences and accommodations, performance management, contingent workers, compensation, privacy, immigration, and export control compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are an experienced attorney&amp;nbsp; who brings strategic thinking, strong program management, and a bias toward action and:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You’re experienced. &lt;/strong&gt;You have 7+ years of combined law firm and in-house experience focused on employment law, including extensive experience in California. Experience scaling a fast growing company nationally and internationally is a plus. Experience at private and public companies is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You’re renowned for your judgment. &lt;/strong&gt;You have a proven combination of great legal instincts and business acumen. You’re comfortable making the big calls regarding legal risk.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You thrive in fast-paced environments, expertly juggling multiple tasks. &lt;/strong&gt;You’re excited about working at an AV company operating on public roads across the globe and pride yourself on just getting stuff done - clearing the way for the business to move fast and scale.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You see opportunity in ambiguity. &lt;/strong&gt;You have experience in spaces where law and regulation is ambiguous, unarticulated, or entirely absent.&amp;nbsp; You are able to identify not just requirements for compliance, but opportunities to lead and define best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You know how to engage with teams and their leaders. &lt;/strong&gt;You are expert in helping other team leaders deliver on their priorities on account of your practical approach to providing legal advice and hustle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You’re a fast and precise writer. &lt;/strong&gt;You are comfortable taking first pen on documents in a range of legal and compliance contexts; able to tailor your writing to audiences; and quickly produce written product that is polished and ready for commercial, public, government, or other external consumption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You care deeply about impact. &lt;/strong&gt;You are passionate that your work makes a significant impact on the lives of millions of people — and recognize the responsibility that comes with it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are technically proficient, and at least as comfortable working with modern tools like AI as you are working manually.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You’re a member of the California Bar.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Admission in other jurisdictions is also a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Nuro, your base pay is one part of your total compensation package. For this position, the reasonably expected base pay range is between $235,000 and $352,000 for the level at which this job has been scoped. Your base pay will depend on several factors, including your experience, qualifications, education, location, and skills. In the event that you are considered for a different level, a higher or lower pay range would apply. This position is also eligible for an annual performance bonus, equity, and a competitive benefits package.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At Nuro, we celebrate differences and are committed to a diverse workplace that fosters inclusion and psychological safety for all employees. Nuro is proud to be an equal opportunity employer and expressly prohibits any form of workplace discrimination based on race, color, religion, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, age, genetic information, disability, veteran status, or any other legally protected characteristics. #LI-CD1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;","departments":[{"id":58168,"name":"Legal","child_ids":[],"parent_id":68794}],"offices":[{"id":23484,"name":"California - HQ","location":"Nuro HQ - Mountain View, CA","child_ids":[],"parent_id":83166}],"ai_disclaimer":null,"include_ai_disclaimer":false,"ai_opt_out_request_url":"http://app.greenhouse.io/ai_opt_out_request/job_post/8227642/ai_opt_out"},{"absolute_url":"https://nuro.ai/careersitem?gh_jid=7325349","data_compliance":[{"type":"gdpr","requires_consent":false,"requires_processing_consent":false,"requires_retention_consent":false,"retention_period":null,"demographic_data_consent_applies":false}],"internal_job_id":3071724,"location":{"name":"Mountain View, California (HQ)"},"metadata":[{"id":53829309,"name":"Location","value":"California - HQ","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":4977510,"name":"Department","value":"Systems","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":954897,"name":"Job Family","value":"SW Systems Engineering","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":4993730,"name":"Time Type","value":"Full-time","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":4978502,"name":"Worker Sub-Type","value":"Regular","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":6653805,"name":"Department (Job Board)","value":"Systems","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":6644840,"name":"Org (Job Board)","value":"Software","value_type":"single_select"}],"id":7325349,"updated_at":"2026-10-09T11:02:43-04:00","requisition_id":"R-101832","title":"Autonomous Driving System Safety Lead","company_name":"Nuro","first_published":"2025-10-13T23:56:27-04:00","language":"en","application_deadline":null,"content":"&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nuro believes self-driving vehicles are the most immediate and profound opportunity for AI to drive positive change in the physical world. Safer streets, more time for what matters, and easier access to the world around us, that’s why we’re building a universal autonomy platform: self-driving for all roads and all rides.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Founded in 2016, Nuro is a physical AI company developing Level 4 autonomous driving technology for a wide range of vehicles, use cases, and markets. Powered by the Nuro Driver™, our universal autonomy platform enables the global mobility ecosystem to deploy autonomy at scale, from robotaxis and logistics fleets to personal vehicles.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;With years of real-world deployment experience and a flexible, partner-led business model, Nuro is working toward a future where millions of autonomous vehicles powered by our technology help make everyday life safer, easier, and more connected.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Nuro has raised over $2B in capital from Uber, NVIDIA, Google, Softbank, Fidelity, T. Rowe Price, and other leading investors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the Autonomous Driving System Safety Lead on the Systems Engineering team, you will own and author safety claims in the forward-facing ADS safety case for onboard and offboard software, a large fraction of which is AI components. You will work closely with the autonomy software, data platform, operations, and legal teams to coordinate system requirements, AI architecture, and evidence in support of these claims. You will be responsible for ensuring that the cross-functional team creates a safety case for onboard and offboard software that is comprehensive and that potential gaps are identified and mitigated.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Work&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage safety claims by understanding the ADS design, interfaces, and technical capabilities of the system and by working closely with Autonomy Robotics and Software Infrastructure leads.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generate atomic claims through claim decomposition, delegating to the cross-functional teams where appropriate and managing quality where delegated.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generate counter-arguments (challenges) to claims, and ensure that they are either addressed or mitigated.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review and assess evidence from evaluation and validation as arguments for safety case claims, and by working closely with V&amp;amp;V test teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop processes for and coordinate the tracking of safety performance indicators, as available from various Systems Engineering and Software Evaluation teams, to monitor driverless (driver-out L4) deployment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Escalate functional and technical risks, and missing work items such as test gaps, ADS design risks, and AI architecture insufficiencies to senior leadership and propose mitigations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support safety research, identify appropriate technical standards and best practices that support the safety case, and apply them effectively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;While this role starts as an individual contributor, there is opportunity to grow a team after the initially defined technical milestones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of technical work experience in a relevant area, of which 3+ years should be in robotics software.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s Degree, Master’s Degree, or Doctoral Degree in Computer Science, Math, Electrical Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, Robotics, Physics, or related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of and ability to apply systems engineering concepts of requirements, verification, and validation, with a deep understanding of how robotic systems work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong quantitative analytical skills and Python experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in a safety-critical industry (e.g. robotics, automotive, aviation/aerospace, medical devices) for a complex robotic system.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with ISO 21448 and familiarity with ISO 8800.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly collaborative in nature with strong abilities to think and communicate analytically and effectively, and the ability to build good working relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Points&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in autonomous vehicles ideally with L4 AV deployment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience writing safety claims and system requirements for SAE L2/L3/L4 systems to operate safely.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with ISO 8800.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with naturalistic driving data and human benchmarking analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with simulation of autonomous vehicles applied to verification and validation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical and strategic management experience with a small team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Nuro, your base pay is one part of your total compensation package. For this position, the reasonably expected base pay range is between $213,480 and $319,720 for the levels at which this job has been scoped. Your base pay will depend on several factors, including your experience, qualifications, education, location, and skills. In the event that you are considered for a different level, a higher or lower pay range would apply. This position is also eligible for an annual performance bonus, equity, and a competitive benefits package.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At Nuro, we celebrate differences and are committed to a diverse workplace that fosters inclusion and psychological safety for all employees. Nuro is proud to be an equal opportunity employer and expressly prohibits any form of workplace discrimination based on race, color, religion, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, age, genetic information, disability, veteran status, or any other legally protected characteristics.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;","departments":[{"id":74129,"name":"Systems","child_ids":[],"parent_id":247412}],"offices":[{"id":23484,"name":"California - HQ","location":"Nuro HQ - Mountain View, CA","child_ids":[],"parent_id":83166}],"ai_disclaimer":null,"include_ai_disclaimer":false,"ai_opt_out_request_url":"http://app.greenhouse.io/ai_opt_out_request/job_post/7325349/ai_opt_out"},{"absolute_url":"https://nuro.ai/careersitem?gh_jid=8104145","data_compliance":[{"type":"gdpr","requires_consent":false,"requires_processing_consent":false,"requires_retention_consent":false,"retention_period":null,"demographic_data_consent_applies":false}],"internal_job_id":3510861,"location":{"name":"California - SF"},"metadata":[{"id":53829309,"name":"Location","value":"California - SF Depot","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":4977510,"name":"Department","value":"In-Vehicle Operations","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":954897,"name":"Job Family","value":"In-Vehicle Operations","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":4993730,"name":"Time Type","value":"Full-time","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":4978502,"name":"Worker Sub-Type","value":"Temporary","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":6653805,"name":"Department (Job Board)","value":"In-Vehicle Operations","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":6644840,"name":"Org (Job Board)","value":"Operations","value_type":"single_select"}],"id":8104145,"updated_at":"2026-10-22T21:09:07-04:00","requisition_id":"M-2036","title":"Autonomous Vehicle Operator","company_name":"Nuro","first_published":"2026-08-03T23:39:38-04:00","language":"en","application_deadline":null,"content":"&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location: &lt;/strong&gt;South San Francisco, CA 94080&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work arrangement: &lt;/strong&gt;Full-time, on-site&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Employment type: &lt;/strong&gt;12-month temporary assignment&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pay:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;$27-$33.25 per hour &lt;em&gt;(Based on shift and day of week, details in compensation section)&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shift:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Afternoon/Evening: 2pm-10:30pm PT&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Overnight: 10pm-6:30am PT&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What to Expect&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Nuro, safety is our guiding principle and our promise—every mile matters as we drive autonomy forward. As an Autonomous Vehicle Operator, you bring this commitment to life through the care, judgment, and accountability you demonstrate on every drive.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll play a critical role in advancing self-driving technology by operating test vehicles in manual and autonomous modes for up to eight hours a day across a variety of real-world traffic and road conditions. You’ll use Nuro’s software and equipment to collect data and provide detailed feedback that helps our engineering teams build safer, more reliable self-driving technology.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Nuro&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nuro believes self-driving vehicles are the most immediate and profound opportunity for AI to drive positive change in the physical world. Safer streets, more time for what matters, and easier access to the world around us, that’s why we’re building a universal autonomy platform: self-driving for all roads and all rides.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Founded in 2016, Nuro is a physical AI company developing Level 4 autonomous driving technology for a wide range of vehicles, use cases, and markets. Powered by the Nuro Driver™, our universal autonomy platform enables the global mobility ecosystem to deploy autonomy at scale, from robotaxis and logistics fleets to personal vehicles.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;With years of real-world deployment experience and a flexible, partner-led business model, Nuro is working toward a future where millions of autonomous vehicles powered by our technology help make everyday life safer, easier, and more connected.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Nuro has raised over $2B in capital from Uber, NVIDIA, Google, Softbank, Fidelity, T. Rowe Price, and other leading investors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive Nuro test vehicles in manual and autonomous modes for up to eight hours a day while following all safety and driving procedures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor the vehicle’s safety, navigation, and driving systems while staying alert to traffic, pedestrians, bicyclists, weather, and road conditions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collect real-world driving data using Nuro’s cutting-edge software and share feedback with engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Complete vehicle checks before and after each shift, report problems, and perform basic upkeep such as washing vehicles and checking tire pressure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot operational issues and coordinate with Mission Operations (dispatch) to resolve problems safely&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use laptops, tablets, smartphones, and other tools to complete reports and document your work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Occasionally speak with members of the public or support ridealongs for company leaders, investors, engineers, and other guests&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;To Be Considered, You&#39;ll Need to&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Always practice safe driving and follow detailed procedures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be available five days per week on the fixed shift you select when you apply&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meet the driving-record requirements below and pass a background check and drug screen&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay focused and observant while sitting and driving for long periods&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate clearly in writing and verbally, and be comfortable using modern online collaboration platforms&amp;nbsp; (e.g., Slack, Google Meet, or similar)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay calm, solve problems, and work independently&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain reliable attendance and arrive on time consistently&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Working Conditions and Essential Functions&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Due to the nature of the position, this job requires:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sitting for 3 to 4 hours at a time for up to 8 hours per day in an enclosed vehicle alone or occasionally with a co-driver&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bending, squatting, stretching and lifting up to 25 pounds on a regular basis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Side and up/down movement of the head, neck, back and shoulders necessary to operate a vehicle safely&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work in a vehicle that may brake, swerve, slow, or stop abruptly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Holding and grasping with hands and frequent use of foot/feet to operate foot pedals when driving the vehicle&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pre-Employment Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must have a current valid California driver’s license and at least three consecutive years of U.S. driving history&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a clean driving record and can pass a criminal background check and drug test&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must meet and maintain all applicable driving record requirements and qualify for an Autonomous Vehicle Tester (AVT) license where required by state law&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensations and Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AM and PM shift pay: &lt;/strong&gt;$27 per hour&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overnight shift pay&lt;/strong&gt;: $28.25&amp;nbsp;per hour&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Weekend differential: &lt;/strong&gt;Employees will receive a $5/per hour incremental weekend differential for hours worked on Saturdays and Sundays, in addition to their base hourly rate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Additional compensation: &lt;/strong&gt;You may also be eligible for a discretionary contract completion bonus based on individual and company performance&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pay schedule:&lt;/strong&gt; Paid every two weeks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Health coverage: &lt;/strong&gt;Medical, dental, and vision insurance beginning on day one&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Paid time off: &lt;/strong&gt;PTO is available, along with company holidays&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Daily lunch reimbursement: &lt;/strong&gt;All Nuro employees receive daily meal reimbursement&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Nuro, we celebrate differences and are committed to a diverse workplace that fosters inclusion and psychological safety for all employees. Nuro is proud to be an equal opportunity employer and expressly prohibits any form of workplace discrimination based on race, color, religion, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, age, genetic information, disability, veteran status, or any other legally protected characteristics.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
