&lt;p&gt;Nuro believes self-driving vehicles are the most immediate and profound opportunity for AI to drive positive change in the physical world. Safer streets, more time for what matters, and easier access to the world around us, that’s why we’re building a universal autonomy platform: self-driving for all roads and all rides.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Founded in 2016, Nuro is a physical AI company developing Level 4 autonomous driving technology for a wide range of vehicles, use cases, and markets. Powered by the Nuro Driver™, our universal autonomy platform enables the global mobility ecosystem to deploy autonomy at scale, from robotaxis and logistics fleets to personal vehicles.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;With years of real-world deployment experience and a flexible, partner-led business model, Nuro is working toward a future where millions of autonomous vehicles powered by our technology help make everyday life safer, easier, and more connected.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Nuro has raised over $2B in capital from Uber, NVIDIA, Google, Softbank, Fidelity, T. Rowe Price, and other leading investors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nuro Driver is the engineering organization that builds the foundational, end-to-end models powering our autonomous driving system, validates their safety, and makes sure they run efficiently onboard our vehicles. That spans Autonomy, Controls, Systems, and Localization, and the people we hire here define what our technology is capable of.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a hands-on recruiting manager to build the team behind that. You will lead 4-5 recruiters and personally run the most important searches, from ML and autonomy to systems engineering and beyond. Expect to spend roughly 50% your time directly running critical searches and 50% building and managing the recruiting team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work side by side with engineering leaders and a deeply technical co-CEO who all care deeply about talent density and treat recruiting as a core part of how we win. You will have real influence over who joins, a direct line to the people making those decisions, and the chance to build the recruiting function for one of the most exciting engineering organizations in autonomy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Own&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hiring strategy and execution for Nuro Driver across ML, autonomy, systems engineering, controls, and localization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leadership and key-hire searches, run personally from sourcing through close&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A team of 4-5 recruiters, including hiring, coaching, workload, and performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Quarterly hiring plans tied to engineering priorities, with clear capacity, timelines, and tradeoffs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pipeline and funnel metrics, reviewed weekly with engineering leaders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner directly with engineering directors, VPs, and the co-CEO to define role scope, sharpen the profile, and decide where the real talent pool sits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Map the market for niche skill sets (perception, planning, prediction, ML infrastructure, state estimation, sensor calibration, safety-critical systems) and build target lists by company, lab, and team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run senior searches personally and close candidates who are choosing between multiple strong offers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach recruiters on sourcing depth, technical screening, and selling the mission to people who are hard to impress&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Calibrate with hiring managers on bar, interview design, and decision speed, and push back when the process is losing candidates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the reporting engineers actually trust: pipeline health, conversion by stage, time to offer, offer acceptance, source quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Total Rewards on offer strategy and competing offers for high-demand profiles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years in technical recruiting, with at least 3 hiring ML, robotics, autonomy, or similarly specialized engineering talent&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years managing recruiters, ideally while still carrying your own searches&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience hiring Staff, Principal, and Director + level engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A working understanding of the Autonomy or ML talent market: who is moving, who is not, what key talent care about, and how compensation in offers is set&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The technical fluency to hold a credible conversation with a software engineer or research scientist, and to tell a strong candidate from a polished one&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A data-first approach. You know your team’s funnel numbers, you can explain why they moved, and you act on them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong judgment in competitive closes, including candidates holding offers from top startups and big tech&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Desire to build a true partnership with engineering leaders, including: advising on how to build the right hiring process, how to sell and pitch, and how to ensure we keep a high talent bar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Points&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience at an AV, robotics, ML, or frontier AI company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience tackling recruiting problems with outside of the box thinking and recommendations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Nuro, your base pay is one part of your total compensation package. For this position, the reasonably expected base pay range is between $160,000 and $240,000 for the level at which this job has been scoped. Your base pay will depend on several factors, including your experience, qualifications, education, location, and skills. In the event that you are considered for a different level, a higher or lower pay range would apply. This position is also eligible for an annual performance bonus, equity, and a competitive benefits package.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At Nuro, we celebrate differences and are committed to a diverse workplace that fosters inclusion and psychological safety for all employees. Nuro is proud to be an equal opportunity employer and expressly prohibits any form of workplace discrimination based on race, color, religion, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, age, genetic information, disability, veteran status, or any other legally protected characteristics. #LI-DNP&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;","departments":[{"id":58203,"name":"Recruiting","child_ids":[],"parent_id":36773}],"offices":[{"id":23484,"name":"California - HQ","location":"Nuro HQ - Mountain View, CA","child_ids":[],"parent_id":83166}],"ai_disclaimer":null,"include_ai_disclaimer":false,"ai_opt_out_request_url":"http://app.greenhouse.io/ai_opt_out_request/job_post/8263630/ai_opt_out"},{"absolute_url":"https://nuro.ai/careersitem?gh_jid=8187498","data_compliance":[{"type":"gdpr","requires_consent":false,"requires_processing_consent":false,"requires_retention_consent":false,"retention_period":null,"demographic_data_consent_applies":false}],"internal_job_id":3542950,"location":{"name":"Mountain View, California (HQ)"},"metadata":[{"id":53829309,"name":"Location","value":"California - HQ","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":4977510,"name":"Department","value":"AV Hardware Engineering","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":954897,"name":"Job Family","value":"Mechanical Design Engineering","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":4993730,"name":"Time Type","value":"Full-time","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":4978502,"name":"Worker Sub-Type","value":"Regular","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":6653805,"name":"Department (Job Board)","value":"AV Hardware Engineering","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":6644840,"name":"Org (Job Board)","value":"Hardware & Manufacturing","value_type":"single_select"}],"id":8187498,"updated_at":"2026-10-09T11:02:43-04:00","requisition_id":"R-103101","title":"AV Hardware Mechanical Engineer","company_name":"Nuro","first_published":"2026-09-09T13:18:41-04:00","language":"en","application_deadline":null,"content":"&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nuro believes self-driving vehicles are the most immediate and profound opportunity for AI to drive positive change in the physical world. Safer streets, more time for what matters, and easier access to the world around us, that’s why we’re building a universal autonomy platform: self-driving for all roads and all rides.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Founded in 2016, Nuro is a physical AI company developing Level 4 autonomous driving technology for a wide range of vehicles, use cases, and markets. Powered by the Nuro Driver™, our universal autonomy platform enables the global mobility ecosystem to deploy autonomy at scale, from robotaxis and logistics fleets to personal vehicles.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;With years of real-world deployment experience and a flexible, partner-led business model, Nuro is working toward a future where millions of autonomous vehicles powered by our technology help make everyday life safer, easier, and more connected.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Nuro has raised over $2B in capital from Uber, NVIDIA, Google, Softbank, Fidelity, T. Rowe Price, and other leading investors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;We are looking for an experienced mechanical designer to join our world class team of engineers in our Autonomous Vehicle Hardware group. In this role you will be responsible for the research, design, and delivery of our autonomous hardware solutions that enable Nuro’s autonomous systems. This work spans electronics and sensor packaging, technology development, and vehicle integrations to support customer programs. You’ll be developing the hardware solutions that safely and reliably enables our L4 autonomy system across platforms, use cases, and operational conditions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Work&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the engineering design, development, and release of autonomous hardware necessary to enable the Nuro Driver system across customer platforms.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the specification and integration in collaboration with our vehicle partners to ensure platform integrations meet the performance needs of our Nuro Driver system and satisfy customer product requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work collaboratively across cross-functional teams to develop and execute sensing and electronics architecture for self-driving robots designed for mass deployment on public roads.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead efforts to benchmark performance, integration, and reliability of available electronics technologies that drives internal make vs. buy decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the identification and key suppliers to bring ideas from concept to production readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage designed parts and assemblies through proof-of-concept validation up through production readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive part quality improvements, cost reductions, and efficiency improvements.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate technical decisions, development plans, and ongoing issues to management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience in mechanical design with a proven track record on design, build, and test of electro-mechanical hardware.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working across the entire production pipeline from personally hand building prototypes to working with quality and manufacturing teams in mass production factory environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using a wide range of manufacturing processes from small scale to high volume, such as rapid prototyping, sheet metal, injection molding, machining, and casting.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing for a wide range of materials with ability to create optimal geometry based on cost, weight, strength/durability, and thermal analysis, using both FEA and hand calculations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with reliability teams to create/execute test plans that validate your designs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with fabrication and module vendors to communicate design requirements, incorporate DFM feedback, manage initial production runs, and oversee validation testing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-starter with strong communication and organizational skills, relentlessly resourceful, with a bias towards action.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with CAD is a must and familiarity with UG NX is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willing and able to support infrequent domestic and international travel.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Nuro, your base pay is one part of your total compensation package. For this position, the reasonably expected base pay range is between $120,270 and $180,410 for the level at which this job has been scoped. Your base pay will depend on several factors, including your experience, qualifications, education, location, and skills. In the event that you are considered for a different level, a higher or lower pay range would apply. This position is also eligible for an annual performance bonus, equity, and a competitive benefits package.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At Nuro, we celebrate differences and are committed to a diverse workplace that fosters inclusion and psychological safety for all employees. Nuro is proud to be an equal opportunity employer and expressly prohibits any form of workplace discrimination based on race, color, religion, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, age, genetic information, disability, veteran status, or any other legally protected characteristics. #LI-DNP&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;","departments":[{"id":87106,"name":"AV Hardware Engineering","child_ids":[],"parent_id":247411}],"offices":[],"ai_disclaimer":null,"include_ai_disclaimer":false,"ai_opt_out_request_url":"http://app.greenhouse.io/ai_opt_out_request/job_post/8187498/ai_opt_out"},{"absolute_url":"https://nuro.ai/careersitem?gh_jid=8044124","data_compliance":[{"type":"gdpr","requires_consent":false,"requires_processing_consent":false,"requires_retention_consent":false,"retention_period":null,"demographic_data_consent_applies":false}],"internal_job_id":3486531,"location":{"name":"Mountain View, California (HQ)"},"metadata":[{"id":53829309,"name":"Location","value":"California - HQ","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":4977510,"name":"Department","value":"Nuro Driver Executives","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":954897,"name":"Job Family","value":"Chief of Staff","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":4993730,"name":"Time Type","value":"Full-time","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":4978502,"name":"Worker Sub-Type","value":"Regular","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":6653805,"name":"Department (Job Board)","value":"Autonomy","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":6644840,"name":"Org (Job Board)","value":"Software","value_type":"single_select"}],"id":8044124,"updated_at":"2026-10-09T11:02:43-04:00","requisition_id":"R-102897","title":"Chief of Staff, Nuro Driver","company_name":"Nuro","first_published":"2026-07-02T13:37:06-04:00","language":"en","application_deadline":null,"content":"&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nuro believes self-driving vehicles are the most immediate and profound opportunity for AI to drive positive change in the physical world. Safer streets, more time for what matters, and easier access to the world around us, that’s why we’re building a universal autonomy platform: self-driving for all roads and all rides.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Founded in 2016, Nuro is a physical AI company developing Level 4 autonomous driving technology for a wide range of vehicles, use cases, and markets. Powered by the Nuro Driver™, our universal autonomy platform enables the global mobility ecosystem to deploy autonomy at scale, from robotaxis and logistics fleets to personal vehicles.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;With years of real-world deployment experience and a flexible, partner-led business model, Nuro is working toward a future where millions of autonomous vehicles powered by our technology help make everyday life safer, easier, and more connected.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Nuro has raised over $2B in capital from Uber, NVIDIA, Google, Softbank, Fidelity, T. Rowe Price, and other leading investors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;As Chief of Staff for Nuro Driver, you will play a critical role in driving strategic programs, improving execution, and helping refine the Autonomy Product that powers Nuro’s commercial partnerships and deployment roadmap.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nuro Driver encompasses Autonomy, Controls, Embedded Software, Sensor Data &amp;amp; Calibration, and Systems Engineering, Technical Program Managers - the core technical functions responsible for developing, integrating, tuning, validating, and scaling the Nuro Driver. Reporting to the VP of Nuro Driver, you will operate as a trusted proxy and execution partner, working across internal engineering teams, company leadership, and key external partners to bring clarity, structure, and momentum to Nuro’s most important technical and business priorities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role requires strong strategic judgment, technical fluency, operational rigor, and executive-level stakeholder management. You will help translate complex product, technical, and partner needs into clear priorities, structured programs, and high-quality execution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Work&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;You will be responsible for driving critical work across Nuro Driver and the company, including:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Program Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead high-priority strategic programs across Nuro Driver, including initiatives tied to autonomy product maturity, partner readiness, deployment milestones, and commercialization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create structure around ambiguous technical and business problems, turning broad goals into clear workstreams, owners, timelines, risks, and decision points.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive cross-organizational initiatives involving Nuro Driver, AI Platform, Vehicle Platform &amp;amp; Hardware, Safety, Operations, Legal, Finance, and People.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with technical leaders to identify critical paths, resolve dependencies, unblock progress, and escalate issues with the right context and urgency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure complex initiatives move from discussion to decision to execution, with clear accountability and follow-through.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Autonomy Product &amp;amp; Partner Execution&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support strategic partner initiatives by coordinating across technical, product, operations, and business stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help define the right forums, processes, and artifacts to align partner expectations with Nuro Driver’s roadmap and execution plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify gaps between partner requirements, internal technical readiness, and deployment milestones, then drive the work needed to close them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;VP of Nuro Driver Proxy &amp;amp; Executive Support&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate as a trusted proxy for the VP of Nuro Driver in key forums, helping drive decisions, clarify priorities, and ensure follow-through.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a strategic filter for the VP, ensuring leadership time and organizational energy are focused on the highest-impact initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare executive-level narratives, updates, and materials for company leadership, Board meetings, partner discussions, planning forums, and strategic reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide insight into organizational execution, leadership effectiveness, operating gaps, and priority tradeoffs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent the VP’s priorities with clarity and judgment while knowing when to escalate, align, or drive independently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nuro Driver Operating Cadence&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve Nuro Driver’s operating cadence across planning, decision-making, communication, and execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Facilitate leadership meetings, technical reviews, milestone reviews, offsites, and cross-functional operating forums.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive clear communication and reporting across all levels of the organization, including leadership updates, all-hands, planning reviews, and company-level forums.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively identify execution risks, organizational gaps, and cross-functional dependencies before they become blockers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help the organization operate with sharper priorities, faster decision-making, and stronger accountability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;People &amp;amp; Organizational Initiatives&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the People Team and Nuro Driver leadership on recruiting, onboarding, performance, talent reviews, engagement, learning and development, and retention initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support organizational design and operating model work as Nuro Driver scales across autonomy, embedded software, controls, calibration, systems, validation, and commercial milestones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help reinforce a high-performance technical culture centered on ownership, speed, quality, accountability, and clear decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;You have 7+ years of experience in technical program management, business operations, product/program management, engineering operations, management consulting, corporate strategy, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;You have experience working closely with engineering teams, ideally in robotics, autonomy, embedded systems, controls, calibration, systems engineering, AI, automotive, or another complex product development environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;You have a track record of driving complex, high-impact programs across multiple teams, senior stakeholders, and ambiguous problem spaces, proactively creating structure and turning strategy into rigorous execution in fast-moving environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;You can quickly understand technical and product context, identify what matters, and translate complexity into clear, actionable decisions and communication, both written and verbal.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;You are comfortable acting as a proxy for senior engineering leadership representing priorities, building trust across technical and non-technical partners (engineering, product, operations, finance, legal, people, and executive teams), driving alignment, and influencing without direct authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2&quot;&gt;You have experience preparing materials for executive audiences, partner discussions, Board meetings, or senior leadership forums.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Points&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting customer-facing or partner-facing technical programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing stakeholders across multiple offices, companies, and time zones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;MBA, experience working at a top consulting firm, or similar experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in using AI tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Nuro, your base pay is one part of your total compensation package. For this position, the reasonably expected base pay range is between $193,930 and $291,150 for the level at which this job has been scoped. Your base pay will depend on several factors, including your experience, qualifications, education, location, and skills. In the event that you are considered for a different level, a higher or lower pay range would apply. This position is also eligible for an annual performance bonus, equity, and a competitive benefits package.&lt;/p&gt;
