11:02:43-04:00","requisition_id":"R-103140","title":"Lead Technical Program Manager, AI Platform ","company_name":"Nuro","first_published":"2026-09-24T13:45:56-04:00","language":"en","application_deadline":null,"content":"&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nuro believes self-driving vehicles are the most immediate and profound opportunity for AI to drive positive change in the physical world. Safer streets, more time for what matters, and easier access to the world around us, that’s why we’re building a universal autonomy platform: self-driving for all roads and all rides.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Founded in 2016, Nuro is a physical AI company developing Level 4 autonomous driving technology for a wide range of vehicles, use cases, and markets. Powered by the Nuro Driver™, our universal autonomy platform enables the global mobility ecosystem to deploy autonomy at scale, from robotaxis and logistics fleets to personal vehicles.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;With years of real-world deployment experience and a flexible, partner-led business model, Nuro is working toward a future where millions of autonomous vehicles powered by our technology help make everyday life safer, easier, and more connected.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Nuro has raised over $2B in capital from Uber, NVIDIA, Google, Softbank, Fidelity, T. Rowe Price, and other leading investors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a technically strong, hands-on Manager of Technical Program Management to lead the TPM team supporting Nuro’s AI Platform organization. AI Platform builds the offboard and onboard system that accelerate autonomy development and enable reliable deployment. Its work spans the data flywheel for developing AI systems—from data collection and data mining through training, simulation, and evaluation—as well as onboard firmware, middleware and services, cloud services, and fleet operations tooling.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will develop a team of TPMs and drive complex programs across engineering, product, operations, and external partners. This role combines people leadership with direct ownership of critical programs: understanding the underlying technical problems, shaping clear plans, resolving dependencies, and driving decisions through implementation. Success means faster development, more reliable systems, and readiness to deploy across vehicle platforms and commercial programs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Work&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead and develop the TPM team.&lt;/strong&gt; Set clear expectations for technical depth, ownership, and execution. Coach TPMs, manage performance and career development, hire strong talent, and align team assignments with the highest-priority needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive critical programs directly.&lt;/strong&gt; Personally lead selected programs that require substantial technical judgment or coordination across teams. Turn ambiguous goals into defined scope, milestones, accountable owners, and measurable outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shape priorities and execution plans&lt;/strong&gt;. Partner with engineering and product leaders to connect platform roadmaps to autonomy development and deployment goals. Surface resource constraints, sequence dependencies, and resolve trade-offs across near-term commitments and longer-term platform investments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Resolve technical and organizational blockers.&lt;/strong&gt; Engage in design reviews, integration planning, and issue investigations to understand root causes, challenge assumptions, and drive decisions. Bring the right experts together and ensure decisions translate into completed work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive integration and deployment readiness.&lt;/strong&gt; Coordinate requirements, interfaces, testing, release gates, rollout plans, and operational readiness across onboard software, offboard services, and partner systems. Ensure gaps have clear owners and closure criteria.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Manage execution with external partners.&lt;/strong&gt; Align vehicle manufacturers, technology suppliers, and commercial partners on deliverables, responsibilities, acceptance criteria, and schedules. Resolve dependencies jointly with engineering, product, business, and legal teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Improve how the organization executes.&lt;/strong&gt; Establish practical planning and review processes that make risks and decisions visible. Use metrics to identify bottlenecks and improve reliability, development speed, and operational efficiency. Apply AI tools and automation to reduce repetitive coordination and reporting work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of experience in technical program management, software engineering, systems engineering, or a related technical discipline, including substantial ownership of complex programs spanning multiple teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of direct people-management experience, with demonstrated success developing TPMs or engineers and addressing performance gaps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical depth in at least one relevant area, such as distributed systems, embedded software, ML infrastructure, data platforms, or robotics, with the ability to learn unfamiliar systems quickly and reason across their interfaces.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of delivering ambiguous technical programs from initial definition through integration, release, and operational adoption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and problem-solving skills: able to distinguish symptoms from root causes, test assumptions, and use evidence to guide prioritization and trade-offs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to influence teams without direct authority, resolve disagreements, and communicate technical issues, risks, and decisions clearly to engineers, executives, and external partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sound judgment about when to investigate personally, when to delegate, and how much process a program needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A degree in computer science, engineering, or a related technical field, or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Nuro, your base pay is one part of your total compensation package. For this position, the reasonably expected base pay range is between $176,400 and $264,600 for the level at which this job has been scoped. Your base pay will depend on several factors, including your experience, qualifications, education, location, and skills. In the event that you are considered for a different level, a higher or lower pay range would apply. This position is also eligible for an annual performance bonus, equity, and a competitive benefits package.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At Nuro, we celebrate differences and are committed to a diverse workplace that fosters inclusion and psychological safety for all employees. Nuro is proud to be an equal opportunity employer and expressly prohibits any form of workplace discrimination based on race, color, religion, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, age, genetic information, disability, veteran status, or any other legally protected characteristics. #LI-DNP&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;","departments":[{"id":293801,"name":"Technical Program Management, AI Platform","child_ids":[],"parent_id":247414}],"offices":[],"ai_disclaimer":null,"include_ai_disclaimer":false,"ai_opt_out_request_url":"http://app.greenhouse.io/ai_opt_out_request/job_post/8227051/ai_opt_out"},{"absolute_url":"https://nuro.ai/careersitem?gh_jid=5434059","data_compliance":[{"type":"gdpr","requires_consent":false,"requires_processing_consent":false,"requires_retention_consent":false,"retention_period":null,"demographic_data_consent_applies":false}],"internal_job_id":2699247,"location":{"name":"Mountain View, California (HQ)"},"metadata":[{"id":53829309,"name":"Location","value":null,"value_type":"single_select"},{"id":4977510,"name":"Department","value":"Autonomy","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":954897,"name":"Job Family","value":"Autonomy","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":4993730,"name":"Time Type","value":"Full-time","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":4978502,"name":"Worker Sub-Type","value":"Regular","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":6653805,"name":"Department (Job Board)","value":"Autonomy","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":6644840,"name":"Org (Job Board)","value":"Software","value_type":"single_select"}],"id":5434059,"updated_at":"2026-10-09T11:02:43-04:00","requisition_id":"R-101415","title":"Machine Learning Research Scientist, Behavior Planning and Prediction ","company_name":"Nuro","first_published":"2023-11-03T15:18:28-04:00","language":"en","application_deadline":null,"content":"&lt;h3&gt;Who We Are&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nuro believes self-driving vehicles are the most immediate and profound opportunity for AI to drive positive change in the physical world. Safer streets, more time for what matters, and easier access to the world around us, that’s why we’re building a universal autonomy platform: self-driving for all roads and all rides.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Founded in 2016, Nuro is a physical AI company developing Level 4 autonomous driving technology for a wide range of vehicles, use cases, and markets. Powered by the Nuro Driver™, our universal autonomy platform enables the global mobility ecosystem to deploy autonomy at scale, from robotaxis and logistics fleets to personal vehicles.&lt;br&gt;With years of real-world deployment experience and a flexible, partner-led business model, Nuro is working toward a future where millions of autonomous vehicles powered by our technology help make everyday life safer, easier, and more connected.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Nuro has raised over $2B in capital from Uber, NVIDIA, Google, Softbank, Fidelity, T. Rowe Price, and other leading investors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the Role&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The mandate of the learned behavior team is to use advanced machine learning techniques to accelerate software progress. In this role, you will work closely with the software vertical teams to understand their pain points and explore novel and advanced machine learning methods to solve practical real-world challenging problems. To name a few, using self-supervised learning to learn robust representations, exploring techniques for out-of-distribution detection to solve long tail problems, adjusting reinforcement learning techniques for motion planning, working on trajectory prediction and motion planning, investigating the robustness of models to mitigate uncertainties, or trying to build an end-to-end driving system. If you love solving challenging new problems with a mindset of deriving practical solutions to eventually be used on the vehicle, come join us!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the Work&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work on scalable machine learning based planning and prediction systems to generate safe and feasible trajectories for autonomous driving.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Research generative sequence modeling and sequential decision making. Research backgrounds we are looking for but not limited to are:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Nice to have: Embodied AI for robotics, Causal reasoning, Model interpretability and explainability, Joint prediction and planning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mitigate uncertainties accumulated through interconnected autonomy components.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate across autonomy teams while developing holistic solutions to top autonomy challenges. Understand issues, propose ideas, prioritize work and develop solutions to solve them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Derive practical solutions and deploy them on real-world vehicles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About You&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You have deep expertise and prior experience in some or many of the following areas:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have an M.Sc. or Ph.D. (preferable) focusing on one or more of the following areas: Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence, Mathematics, or a closely related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have subject matter expertise and research in one or more of the following areas: sequential decision making, Imitation Learning, Deep Reinforcement Learning, generative modeling, large models (pretraining/finetuning), machine learning for robotics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have strong problem solving and programming skills in Python (required) and C++ (beneficial)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong culture fit and good team player&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated research publications in top conferences (e.g. NeurIPS, ICLR, ICML, CVPR, RSS, CoRL, ICRA)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Nuro, we celebrate differences and are committed to a diverse workplace that fosters inclusion and psychological safety for all employees. Nuro is proud to be an equal opportunity employer and expressly prohibits any form of workplace discrimination based on race, color, religion, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, age, genetic information, disability, veteran status, or any other legally protected characteristics.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Nuro, your base pay is one part of your total compensation package. For this position, the reasonably expected pay range is between $160,360 and $240,540/ year for the level at which this job has been scoped. Your base pay will depend on several factors, including your experience, qualifications, education, location, and skills. In the event that you are considered for a different level, a higher or lower pay range would apply. This position is also eligible for an annual performance bonus, equity, and a competitive benefits package.&lt;/p&gt;
