&lt;p&gt;Nuro believes self-driving vehicles are the most immediate and profound opportunity for AI to drive positive change in the physical world. Safer streets, more time for what matters, and easier access to the world around us, that’s why we’re building a universal autonomy platform: self-driving for all roads and all rides.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Founded in 2016, Nuro is a physical AI company developing Level 4 autonomous driving technology for a wide range of vehicles, use cases, and markets. Powered by the Nuro Driver™, our universal autonomy platform enables the global mobility ecosystem to deploy autonomy at scale, from robotaxis and logistics fleets to personal vehicles.&lt;br&gt;With years of real-world deployment experience and a flexible, partner-led business model, Nuro is working toward a future where millions of autonomous vehicles powered by our technology help make everyday life safer, easier, and more connected.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Nuro has raised over $2B in capital from Uber, NVIDIA, Google, Softbank, Fidelity, T. Rowe Price, and other leading investors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Work&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and scale state-of-the-art generative models—especially diffusion architectures, flow-matching techniques, and energy-based models —for autonomous plan generation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build generative models with foundation models. Leverage large language models and world foundation models for reasoning, decision making and multi-modality generation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Optimize generative models using reinforcement learning to improve interactive reasoning. Explore reward modeling/learned verifier using generative models. Explore joint prediction and planning and self-play. Leverage generative models for active learning and world modeling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop controllable generative models to guide the generation process towards desired goals, conditions and rewards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate across autonomy teams while developing holistic solutions to top autonomy challenges. Understand issues, propose ideas, prioritize work and develop solutions to solve them, evaluate your solution by deploying the models on to the NuroDriver.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You have deep expertise and prior experience in some or many of the following areas:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a Ph.D. (preferable) or M.Sc. with 2-3 years of experience working with generative models in the lab, in industry, or both.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Research experiences in generative models, particularly diffusion models, flow matching and energy-based models, for robotics, including manipulation, path planning, and autonomous driving. Experiences in vision-language-action models, reinforcement learning for generative model optimization, video generation, text-to-image generation, diffusion models for LLMs, world foundation models, and other applications of generative modeling are a bonus!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have strong problem solving and programming skills in Python and/or C++&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong culture fit and good team player.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated research publications in top conferences (e.g. NeurIPS, ICLR, ICML, CVPR, RSS, CoRL etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Nuro, your base pay is one part of your total compensation package. For this position, the reasonably expected pay range is between $160,360 and $240,540/ year for the level at which this job has been scoped. Your base pay will depend on several factors, including your experience, qualifications, education, location, and skills. In the event that you are considered for a different level, a higher or lower pay range would apply. This position is also eligible for an annual performance bonus, equity, and a competitive benefits package.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At Nuro, we celebrate differences and are committed to a diverse workplace that fosters inclusion and psychological safety for all employees. Nuro is proud to be an equal opportunity employer and expressly prohibits any form of workplace discrimination based on race, color, religion, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, age, genetic information, disability, veteran status, or any other legally protected characteristics.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;","departments":[{"id":216513,"name":"Autonomy","child_ids":[],"parent_id":247412}],"offices":[{"id":23484,"name":"California - HQ","location":"Nuro HQ - Mountain View, CA","child_ids":[],"parent_id":83166}],"ai_disclaimer":null,"include_ai_disclaimer":false,"ai_opt_out_request_url":"http://app.greenhouse.io/ai_opt_out_request/job_post/5416913/ai_opt_out"},{"absolute_url":"https://nuro.ai/careersitem?gh_jid=7439020","data_compliance":[{"type":"gdpr","requires_consent":false,"requires_processing_consent":false,"requires_retention_consent":false,"retention_period":null,"demographic_data_consent_applies":false}],"internal_job_id":3308888,"location":{"name":"Mountain View, California (HQ)"},"metadata":[{"id":53829309,"name":"Location","value":"California - HQ","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":4977510,"name":"Department","value":"Autonomy","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":954897,"name":"Job Family","value":"Autonomy","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":4993730,"name":"Time Type","value":"Full-time","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":4978502,"name":"Worker Sub-Type","value":"Regular","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":6653805,"name":"Department (Job Board)","value":"Autonomy","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":6644840,"name":"Org (Job Board)","value":"Software","value_type":"single_select"}],"id":7439020,"updated_at":"2026-10-09T11:02:43-04:00","requisition_id":"R-102159","title":"ML Research Scientist, Prediction & Smart Agents","company_name":"Nuro","first_published":"2026-02-19T00:31:38-05:00","language":"en","application_deadline":null,"content":"&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nuro believes self-driving vehicles are the most immediate and profound opportunity for AI to drive positive change in the physical world. Safer streets, more time for what matters, and easier access to the world around us, that’s why we’re building a universal autonomy platform: self-driving for all roads and all rides.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Founded in 2016, Nuro is a physical AI company developing Level 4 autonomous driving technology for a wide range of vehicles, use cases, and markets. Powered by the Nuro Driver™, our universal autonomy platform enables the global mobility ecosystem to deploy autonomy at scale, from robotaxis and logistics fleets to personal vehicles.&lt;br&gt;With years of real-world deployment experience and a flexible, partner-led business model, Nuro is working toward a future where millions of autonomous vehicles powered by our technology help make everyday life safer, easier, and more connected.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Nuro has raised over $2B in capital from Uber, NVIDIA, Google, Softbank, Fidelity, T. Rowe Price, and other leading investors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The mandate of the prediction team is to use advanced machine learning techniques to improve the behavior of the Nuro Driver.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a key member of the Prediction and Smart Agents team, you will focus on building state-of-the-art models for predicting the behavior of surrounding traffic. These models are crucial for our autonomous system, as they will be deployed onboard as part of our planning stack and used offboard for realistic closed-loop simulation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will explore novel machine learning methods to solve challenging real-world problems in autonomous driving. This work includes using generative sequence modeling approaches for robustly predicting complex, interactive traffic situations. It requires deep reasoning about the intentions of other road users and how their behaviors influence safe and correct driving decisions. You will also use different input modalities, including End-to-End (E2E) approaches, for predicting other agents. A vital component of this role is building smart, controllable agents to enable effective closed-loop training in simulation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you are passionate about solving challenging new problems, leading impactful research, and seeing your work deployed onto real robots, we encourage you to apply!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Work&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and build scalable, machine learning-based prediction systems to generate multi-modal, realistic, and kinematically feasible trajectories.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct cutting-edge research in generative sequence modeling and sequential decision-making. Areas of interest include, but are not limited to:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scalable generative sequence modeling approaches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Marginal, conditional, and joint distribution modeling for interactive agents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Transformer-based encoder-decoder architectures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Large generative models and diffusion models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Controllability of agents via conditioning, guidance, and other techniques.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with the Planning team to design realistic and controllable agents for closed-loop simulation, enabling agent training via Reinforcement Learning (RL).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mitigate accumulated uncertainties across interconnected autonomy components.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate across various autonomy teams to develop holistic solutions for top challenges, proposing ideas, prioritizing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Derive practical, deployable solutions and see them deployed on real-world vehicles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You have deep expertise and prior experience in some or many of the following areas:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education: &lt;/strong&gt;You have an M.Sc. or Ph.D. (preferable) focusing on one or more of the following areas: Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence, Mathematics, or a closely related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt; Subject matter expertise and research experience in one or more of the following: sequential decision-making, prediction, Imitation Learning, Deep Reinforcement Learning, generative modeling, large models (pretraining/finetuning), or machine learning for robotics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Skills:&lt;/strong&gt; You have strong problem solving and programming skills in Python (required) and C++ (beneficial) and ML frameworks such as PyTorch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaboration:&lt;/strong&gt; Strong culture fit and good team player.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; You have 2+ years of deploying machine learning systems onboard, ideally in the area of prediction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Publications:&lt;/strong&gt; Demonstrated research publications in top conferences (e.g. NeurIPS, ICLR, ICML, CVPR, RSS, CoRL, ICRA, IROS etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have:&lt;/strong&gt; Deep background in Embodied AI for robotics, Causal reasoning, Model interpretability and explainability, Joint prediction and planning, Understanding of Diffusion Models.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Nuro, your base pay is one part of your total compensation package. For this position, the reasonably expected base pay range is between $193,930 and $291,150 for the level at which this job has been scoped. Your base pay will depend on several factors, including your experience, qualifications, education, location, and skills. In the event that you are considered for a different level, a higher or lower pay range would apply. This position is also eligible for an annual performance bonus, equity, and a competitive benefits package.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At Nuro, we celebrate differences and are committed to a diverse workplace that fosters inclusion and psychological safety for all employees. Nuro is proud to be an equal opportunity employer and expressly prohibits any form of workplace discrimination based on race, color, religion, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, age, genetic information, disability, veteran status, or any other legally protected characteristics. #LI-DNP&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;","departments":[{"id":216513,"name":"Autonomy","child_ids":[],"parent_id":247412}],"offices":[{"id":23484,"name":"California - HQ","location":"Nuro HQ - Mountain View, CA","child_ids":[],"parent_id":83166}],"ai_disclaimer":null,"include_ai_disclaimer":false,"ai_opt_out_request_url":"http://app.greenhouse.io/ai_opt_out_request/job_post/7439020/ai_opt_out"},{"absolute_url":"https://nuro.ai/careersitem?gh_jid=8259036","data_compliance":[{"type":"gdpr","requires_consent":false,"requires_processing_consent":false,"requires_retention_consent":false,"retention_period":null,"demographic_data_consent_applies":false}],"internal_job_id":3573696,"location":{"name":"California - SF"},"metadata":[{"id":53829309,"name":"Location","value":"California - Santa Clara","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":4977510,"name":"Department","value":"In-Vehicle Operations","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":954897,"name":"Job Family","value":"In-Vehicle Operations","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":4993730,"name":"Time Type","value":"Full-time","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":4978502,"name":"Worker Sub-Type","value":"Temporary","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":6653805,"name":"Department (Job Board)","value":"In-Vehicle Operations","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":6644840,"name":"Org (Job Board)","value":"Operations","value_type":"single_select"}],"id":8259036,"updated_at":"2026-10-22T21:05:19-04:00","requisition_id":"M-2102","title":"On-Site Hiring Event: Autonomous Vehicle Operator, San Francisco ","company_name":"Nuro","first_published":"2026-10-06T23:11:45-04:00","language":"en","application_deadline":null,"content":"&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This position is based on-site in South San Francisco, CA. The hiring event will be held in Santa Clara, CA 95054&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work arrangement: &lt;/strong&gt;Full-time, on-site&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Employment type: &lt;/strong&gt;12-month temporary assignment&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pay:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;$27-$33.25 per hour &lt;em&gt;(Based on shift and day of week, details in compensation section)&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shifts:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Morning/Afternoon: 6am-2:30pm PT&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Afternoon/Evening: 2pm-10:30pm PT&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Overnight: 10pm-6:30am PT&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re hosting an&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;on-site hiring event from 9:30am-4pm PT on Thursday, October 29 2026, in Santa Clara, CA 95054.&lt;/strong&gt; If you love driving and want to work hands on with groundbreaking autonomous vehicle technology, this role is for you!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;How to attend:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Apply first!&lt;/strong&gt; After reading through the job description please submit your application below.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Get the details!&lt;/strong&gt; We will follow up soon after you apply with the &lt;strong&gt;full event agenda and exact location&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;to find a time that works best for you.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What to Expect&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Nuro, safety is our guiding principle and our promise—every mile matters as we drive autonomy forward. As an Autonomous Vehicle Operator, you bring this commitment to life through the care, judgment, and accountability you demonstrate on every drive.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll play a critical role in advancing self-driving technology by operating test vehicles in manual and autonomous modes for up to eight hours a day across a variety of real-world traffic and road conditions. You’ll use Nuro’s software and equipment to collect data and provide detailed feedback that helps our engineering teams build safer, more reliable self-driving technology.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Nuro&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nuro believes self-driving vehicles are the most immediate and profound opportunity for AI to drive positive change in the physical world. Safer streets, more time for what matters, and easier access to the world around us, that’s why we’re building a universal autonomy platform: self-driving for all roads and all rides.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Founded in 2016, Nuro is a physical AI company developing Level 4 autonomous driving technology for a wide range of vehicles, use cases, and markets. Powered by the Nuro Driver™, our universal autonomy platform enables the global mobility ecosystem to deploy autonomy at scale, from robotaxis and logistics fleets to personal vehicles.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;With years of real-world deployment experience and a flexible, partner-led business model, Nuro is working toward a future where millions of autonomous vehicles powered by our technology help make everyday life safer, easier, and more connected.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Nuro has raised over $2B in capital from Uber, NVIDIA, Google, Softbank, Fidelity, T. Rowe Price, and other leading investors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive Nuro test vehicles in manual and autonomous modes for up to eight hours a day while following all safety and driving procedures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor the vehicle’s safety, navigation, and driving systems while staying alert to traffic, pedestrians, bicyclists, weather, and road conditions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collect real-world driving data using Nuro’s cutting-edge software and share feedback with engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Complete vehicle checks before and after each shift, report problems, and perform basic upkeep such as washing vehicles and checking tire pressure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot operational issues and coordinate with Mission Operations (dispatch) to resolve problems safely&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use laptops, tablets, smartphones, and other tools to complete reports and document your work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Occasionally speak with members of the public or support ridealongs for company leaders, investors, engineers, and other guests&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;To Be Considered, You&#39;ll Need to&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Always practice safe driving and follow detailed procedures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be available five days per week on the fixed shift you select when you apply&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meet the driving-record requirements below and pass a background check and drug screen&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay focused and observant while sitting and driving for long periods&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate clearly in writing and verbally, and be comfortable using modern online collaboration platforms&amp;nbsp; (e.g., Slack, Google Meet, or similar)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay calm, solve problems, and work independently&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain reliable attendance and arrive on time consistently&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Working Conditions and Essential Functions&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Due to the nature of the position, this job requires:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sitting for 3 to 4 hours at a time for up to 8 hours per day in an enclosed vehicle alone or occasionally with a co-driver&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bending, squatting, stretching and lifting up to 25 pounds on a regular basis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Side and up/down movement of the head, neck, back and shoulders necessary to operate a vehicle safely&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work in a vehicle that may brake, swerve, slow, or stop abruptly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Holding and grasping with hands and frequent use of foot/feet to operate foot pedals when driving the vehicle&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pre-Employment Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must have a current valid California driver’s license and at least three consecutive years of U.S. driving history&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a clean driving record and can pass a criminal background check and drug test&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must meet and maintain all applicable driving record requirements and qualify for an Autonomous Vehicle Tester (AVT) license where required by state law&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensations and Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AM and PM shift pay: &lt;/strong&gt;$27 per hour&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overnight shift pay&lt;/strong&gt;: $28.25&amp;nbsp;per hour&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Weekend differential: &lt;/strong&gt;Employees will receive a weekend differential for hours worked on Saturdays and Sundays, in addition to their base hourly rate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Additional compensation: &lt;/strong&gt;You may also be eligible for a discretionary contract completion bonus based on individual and company performance&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pay schedule:&lt;/strong&gt; Paid every two weeks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Health coverage: &lt;/strong&gt;Medical, dental, and vision insurance beginning on day one&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Paid time off: &lt;/strong&gt;PTO is available, along with company holidays&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Daily lunch reimbursement: &lt;/strong&gt;All Nuro employees receive daily meal reimbursement&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Nuro, we celebrate differences and are committed to a diverse workplace that fosters inclusion and psychological safety for all employees. Nuro is proud to be an equal opportunity employer and expressly prohibits any form of workplace discrimination based on race, color, religion, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, age, genetic information, disability, veteran status, or any other legally protected characteristics.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;","departments":[{"id":64841,"name":"In-Vehicle Operations","child_ids":[],"parent_id":61614}],"offices":[{"id":306393,"name":"California - South SF Depot ","location":"California, United States","child_ids":[],"parent_id":83166}],"ai_disclaimer":null,"include_ai_disclaimer":false,"ai_opt_out_request_url":"http://app.greenhouse.io/ai_opt_out_request/job_post/8259036/ai_opt_out"},{"absolute_url":"https://nuro.ai/careersitem?gh_jid=8138188","data_compliance":[{"type":"gdpr","requires_consent":false,"requires_processing_consent":false,"requires_retention_consent":false,"retention_period":null,"demographic_data_consent_applies":false}],"internal_job_id":3522190,"location":{"name":"Mountain View, California (HQ)"},"metadata":[{"id":53829309,"name":"Location","value":null,"value_type":"single_select"},{"id":4977510,"name":"Department","value":"Autonomy Platform","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":954897,"name":"Job Family","value":"Autonomy/ML Platform","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":4993730,"name":"Time Type","value":"Full-time","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":4978502,"name":"Worker Sub-Type","value":"Regular","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":6653805,"name":"Department (Job Board)","value":"Partnerships","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":6644840,"name":"Org (Job Board)","value":"Commercialization","value_type":"single_select"}],"id":8138188,"updated_at":"2026-10-09T11:02:43-04:00","requisition_id":"R-103018","title":"Partnerships Lead","company_name":"Nuro","first_published":"2026-08-24T22:30:06-04:00","language":"en","application_deadline":null,"content":"&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nuro believes self-driving vehicles are the most immediate and profound opportunity for AI to drive positive change in the physical world. Safer streets, more time for what matters, and easier access to the world around us, that’s why we’re building a universal autonomy platform: self-driving for all roads and all rides.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Founded in 2016, Nuro is a physical AI company developing Level 4 autonomous driving technology for a wide range of vehicles, use cases, and markets. Powered by the Nuro Driver™, our universal autonomy platform enables the global mobility ecosystem to deploy autonomy at scale, from robotaxis and logistics fleets to personal vehicles.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;With years of real-world deployment experience and a flexible, partner-led business model, Nuro is working toward a future where millions of autonomous vehicles powered by our technology help make everyday life safer, easier, and more connected.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Nuro has raised over $2B in capital from Uber, NVIDIA, Google, Softbank, Fidelity, T. Rowe Price, and other leading investors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nuro is looking for a senior partnerships and relationship management professional to own many of the key relationships that our technology depends on. Building the Nuro Driver requires a number of deep partnerships across cloud and compute providers, silicon, Tier 1 suppliers, and OEMs. Building the Nuro Driver requires a number of deep partnerships across cloud and compute providers, silicon, Tier 1 suppliers, and OEMs. This role builds and manages those relationships.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is not traditional business development. We are not chasing a high volume of new logos, and we say no to more deals than we say yes to. The work involves holding a small set of critical relationships at the senior and executive level over years, keeping commercial agreements current, and making sure the internal follow through actually happens. You will work closely with our Founders and Executive Team, our existing partnership team focused on new commercial opportunities, and with our Supply Chain Team, which owns parts and schedules.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a senior-level individual contributor role. Success looks like partners who know exactly who to call at Nuro, agreements that get renewed on good terms before they become urgent, and problems that get resolved before they reach the co-CEOs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Work&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own senior and executive level relationships with Nuro&#39;s existing cloud, compute, Tier 1, and OEM partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the first escalation point when a partner relationship goes sideways, and resolve it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead commercial terms, renewals, and amendments on existing agreements, working with business development, legal, engineering and finance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run the internal follow through: track what was committed on both sides, drive the cross functional work, and keep partners current on what is happening and when&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hold a clear view of where each relationship stands, what it is worth to Nuro, and where it should go over the next two to three years&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare clear, executive ready materials that communicate recommendations, tradeoffs, and deal rationale, for internal review and for partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with business development on new opportunities that come out of existing relationships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Approximately 7+ years of experience, starting in management consulting, investment banking, or corporate strategy, with meaningful time since then in an operating role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have held a senior partner or customer relationship across multiple years, not a single transaction. You can name the counterpart and say what changed because you were the person holding it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deal credibility. You have been in the room for commercial negotiations and can carry that conversation yourself.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Organized enough that it is a differentiator. You know what was promised, by whom, and when it is due, across a lot of moving parts, across multiple partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to learn technical concepts quickly and explain them clearly to a commercial audience, and the reverse&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication with senior audiences, internal and external&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable with ambiguity and willing to take ownership to move work forward with speed and quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Points&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in autonomous systems, automotive, semiconductors, or cloud infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience owning partner relationships at a company that licenses technology rather than selling a finished product&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;MBA from a top university, or a degree in computer science, engineering, or a related technical field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Nuro, your base pay is one part of your total compensation package. For this position, the reasonably expected base pay range is between $176,400 and $264,600 for the level at which this job has been scoped. Your base pay will depend on several factors, including your experience, qualifications, education, location, and skills. In the event that you are considered for a different level, a higher or lower pay range would apply. This position is also eligible for an annual performance bonus, equity, and a competitive benefits package.&lt;/p&gt;
