Nuro","first_published":"2026-10-12T18:52:49-04:00","language":"en","application_deadline":null,"content":"&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nuro is a self-driving technology company on a mission to make autonomy accessible to all. Founded in 2016, Nuro is building the world’s most scalable driver, combining cutting-edge AI with automotive-grade hardware. Nuro licenses its core technology, the Nuro Driver™, to support a wide range of applications, from robotaxis and commercial fleets to personally owned vehicles. With technology proven over years of self-driving deployments, Nuro gives the automakers and mobility platforms a clear path to AVs at commercial scale, empowering a safer, richer, and more connected future.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;As an Infrastructure Security Engineer, you will increase the security of Nuro’s core infrastructure used to develop and operate our autonomous delivery service. You will need to leverage your technical skills to create cross-functional strategic outcomes for Nuro. You will need to use good engineering judgment when evaluating and fixing both real and theoretical vulnerabilities. You work closely with development teams and can build systems. Your work contributes directly to the safety and security of the people in the communities we operate in. You’re a collaborative thinker with an ownership mindset, and thrive in fast-paced and collaborative environments. As a member of Nuro’s Security team, you will work on projects that impact all areas of security, from offensive testing to detection and response.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Work&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assess and secure Nuro and protect user data.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate and verify engineering teams&#39; vulnerability remediations (PR review or other evaluations)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and build security tooling and infrastructure for use Nuro’s engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and implement core security infrastructure like authentication and authorization systems, pipelines and automation for security incident detection and response, PKI, and others&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expert in one or more core domains: Securely using a public cloud, securing corporate networks and endpoints, or application security&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Software development skills, preferably in Python, Go, or C++&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have start-up DNA: You have demonstrated an ability to thrive in the ambiguity of a dynamic, start-up environment or have the DNA to do so&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication, presentation, interpersonal, and analytical skills; the ability to communicate complex interaction concepts and risks clearly and persuasively in a highly eng-driven environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Points&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to exploit vulnerabilities, e.g., winning or placing in Capture the Flags, 0-Days/CVEs, or conference talks on security research.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reverse Engineering software using IDA Pro, Ghidra, Radare, Frida, or other tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Software or hardware development&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Developing Systems Engineering requirements and verification statements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Attacking embedded, real-time, safety, or flight-critical systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CAN, Automotive Ethernet, or other vehicle buses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Physical security assessments&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Automotive systems, especially autonomous vehicles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building, evaluating, designing, and shipping hardware products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scaling Kubernetes and/or Google Cloud security best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Nuro, your base pay is one part of your total compensation package. For this position, the reasonably expected base pay range is between $160,360 and $240,540 for the level at which this job has been scoped. Your base pay will depend on several factors, including your experience, qualifications, education, location, and skills. In the event that you are considered for a different level, a higher or lower pay range would apply. This position is also eligible for an annual performance bonus, equity, and a competitive benefits package.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At Nuro, we celebrate differences and are committed to a diverse workplace that fosters inclusion and psychological safety for all employees. Nuro is proud to be an equal opportunity employer and expressly prohibits any form of workplace discrimination based on race, color, religion, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, age, genetic information, disability, veteran status, or any other legally protected characteristics.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;","departments":[{"id":146802,"name":"Commercialization ","child_ids":[61614,58167,317267,74125,72498,83180,68791,79180,64841,86856,79177,58757],"parent_id":null}],"offices":[{"id":23484,"name":"California - HQ","location":"Nuro HQ - Mountain View, CA","child_ids":[],"parent_id":83166}],"ai_disclaimer":null,"include_ai_disclaimer":false,"ai_opt_out_request_url":"http://app.greenhouse.io/ai_opt_out_request/job_post/7702403/ai_opt_out"},{"absolute_url":"https://nuro.ai/careersitem?gh_jid=8196053","data_compliance":[{"type":"gdpr","requires_consent":false,"requires_processing_consent":false,"requires_retention_consent":false,"retention_period":null,"demographic_data_consent_applies":false}],"internal_job_id":3547075,"location":{"name":"Mountain View, California (HQ)"},"metadata":[{"id":53829309,"name":"Location","value":"California - HQ","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":4977510,"name":"Department","value":"Legal","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":954897,"name":"Job Family","value":"General Counsel","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":4993730,"name":"Time Type","value":"Full-time","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":4978502,"name":"Worker Sub-Type","value":"Regular","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":6653805,"name":"Department (Job Board)","value":"Legal","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":6644840,"name":"Org (Job Board)","value":"Public Trust","value_type":"single_select"}],"id":8196053,"updated_at":"2026-10-09T11:02:43-04:00","requisition_id":"R-103112","title":"Senior Commercial Counsel","company_name":"Nuro","first_published":"2026-09-15T18:11:00-04:00","language":"en","application_deadline":null,"content":"&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nuro believes self-driving vehicles are the most immediate and profound opportunity for AI to drive positive change in the physical world. Safer streets, more time for what matters, and easier access to the world around us, that’s why we’re building a universal autonomy platform: self-driving for all roads and all rides.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Founded in 2016, Nuro is a physical AI company developing Level 4 autonomous driving technology for a wide range of vehicles, use cases, and markets. Powered by the Nuro Driver™, our universal autonomy platform enables the global mobility ecosystem to deploy autonomy at scale, from robotaxis and logistics fleets to personal vehicles.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;With years of real-world deployment experience and a flexible, partner-led business model, Nuro is working toward a future where millions of autonomous vehicles powered by our technology help make everyday life safer, easier, and more connected.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Nuro has raised over $2B in capital from Uber, NVIDIA, Google, Softbank, Fidelity, T. Rowe Price, and other leading investors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;The Legal team is a strategic partner to the business, helping teams move quickly and responsibly as the company scales. We work cross-functionally with supply chain, business development, product, engineering, partnerships, and other groups to enable innovation, manage risk, and build scalable processes. Our team values practical judgment, clear communication, collaboration, and a solutions-oriented approach.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Senior Commercial Counsel, you will advise on the commercial transactions that support our mission and day-to-day operations. You will structure, draft, negotiate, and manage agreements involving vehicle systems and components, intellectual property, strategic partnerships, software and SaaS, professional services, goods and services, non-disclosure agreements, and more.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is ideal for a pragmatic, business-minded attorney who can independently manage matters ranging from routine agreements to complex, groundbreaking transactions. Success requires sound judgment, strong execution, attention to detail, and a collaborative approach to working with teams across the company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Work&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead commercial transactions from intake through post-signature management, partnering with business and technical teams to develop strategies, negotiate with counterparties, and finalize agreements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise on legal and business risks, explain complex terms clearly, and recommend practical, risk-conscious solutions aligned with company objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support matters across supply chain; business development, product, and partnerships; intellectual property and licensing; data privacy and security; marketing; real estate and facilities; and other areas as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Train cross-functional teams on commercial contracting requirements, best practices, and effective risk management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help implement and launch a new contract lifecycle management (CLM) system, including templates, playbooks, fallback positions, workflows, and related process improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Streamline and automate contracting processes to improve efficiency, consistency, and visibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a legal “utility player,” contributing beyond commercial transactions in areas such as intellectual property, privacy, marketing, real estate, and product- or customer-facing matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply AI tools thoughtfully to improve legal workflows, processes, and team efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of legal experience in a fast-growing, technology-focused company, top-tier law firm, or a combination of both, with significant experience independently handling complex commercial transactions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional drafting, negotiation, communication, and stakeholder-management skills, including the ability to produce polished work for executive and external audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience advising high-growth technology businesses and translating complex legal issues into practical, actionable business guidance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of intellectual property, privacy, liability and risk allocation, and supply chain matters; automotive, hardware, or transportation experience is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong legal judgment and business acumen, with the ability to assess risk, present clear options, and make accountable recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage multiple priorities independently, build trust with business leaders, and distinguish urgent issues from those that are most important.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execution-oriented and resourceful, with a demonstrated ability to drive processes forward, overcome obstacles, conduct rigorous research, and deliver results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative, creative, and effective in small, diverse, cross-functional teams, with a commitment to practical problem-solving and meaningful business impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interest in using AI and other tools to improve legal workflows, operational efficiency, and team effectiveness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Admission to at least one state bar required; California Bar membership preferred. Admission in additional jurisdictions is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Nuro, your base pay is one part of your total compensation package. For this position, the reasonably expected base pay range is between $193,000 and $291,000 for the level at which this job has been scoped. Your base pay will depend on several factors, including your experience, qualifications, education, location, and skills. In the event that you are considered for a different level, a higher or lower pay range would apply. This position is also eligible for an annual performance bonus, equity, and a competitive benefits package.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At Nuro, we celebrate differences and are committed to a diverse workplace that fosters inclusion and psychological safety for all employees. Nuro is proud to be an equal opportunity employer and expressly prohibits any form of workplace discrimination based on race, color, religion, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, age, genetic information, disability, veteran status, or any other legally protected characteristics. #LI-CD1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;","departments":[{"id":58168,"name":"Legal","child_ids":[],"parent_id":68794}],"offices":[{"id":23484,"name":"California - HQ","location":"Nuro HQ - Mountain View, CA","child_ids":[],"parent_id":83166}],"ai_disclaimer":null,"include_ai_disclaimer":false,"ai_opt_out_request_url":"http://app.greenhouse.io/ai_opt_out_request/job_post/8196053/ai_opt_out"},{"absolute_url":"https://nuro.ai/careersitem?gh_jid=8263454","data_compliance":[{"type":"gdpr","requires_consent":false,"requires_processing_consent":false,"requires_retention_consent":false,"retention_period":null,"demographic_data_consent_applies":false}],"internal_job_id":3575470,"location":{"name":"Mountain View, California (HQ)"},"metadata":[{"id":53829309,"name":"Location","value":"California - HQ","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":4977510,"name":"Department","value":"Controls, Pose and ESWE","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":954897,"name":"Job Family","value":"Embedded Controls Engineering","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":4993730,"name":"Time Type","value":"Full-time","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":4978502,"name":"Worker Sub-Type","value":"Regular","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":6653805,"name":"Department (Job Board)","value":"Controls, Pose, and Embedded Software","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":6644840,"name":"Org (Job Board)","value":"Software","value_type":"single_select"}],"id":8263454,"updated_at":"2026-10-09T11:02:43-04:00","requisition_id":"R-103176","title":"Senior Embedded Software Engineer","company_name":"Nuro","first_published":"2026-10-08T16:41:07-04:00","language":"en","application_deadline":null,"content":"&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nuro believes self-driving vehicles are the most immediate and profound opportunity for AI to drive positive change in the physical world. Safer streets, more time for what matters, and easier access to the world around us, that’s why we’re building a universal autonomy platform: self-driving for all roads and all rides.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Founded in 2016, Nuro is a physical AI company developing Level 4 autonomous driving technology for a wide range of vehicles, use cases, and markets. Powered by the Nuro Driver™, our universal autonomy platform enables the global mobility ecosystem to deploy autonomy at scale, from robotaxis and logistics fleets to personal vehicles.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;With years of real-world deployment experience and a flexible, partner-led business model, Nuro is working toward a future where millions of autonomous vehicles powered by our technology help make everyday life safer, easier, and more connected.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Nuro has raised over $2B in capital from Uber, NVIDIA, Google, Softbank, Fidelity, T. Rowe Price, and other leading investors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nuro operates real self-driving vehicles on public roads today — not a research platform, not ADAS. The Embedded Software Engineering team builds the software for the safety-critical embedded controllers that connect the Nuro Driver™ to the vehicle: the devices that command steering, braking, and propulsion, alongside other vehicle actuators, distribute and monitor power, monitor vehicle motion, and bring the vehicle to a safe state when something goes wrong.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Embedded Software Engineer, you will work across the full stack of multicore automotive microcontrollers from RTOS, drivers, and scheduler up through middleware and application components that talk to the vehicle, and help extend that stack as our hardware evolves. You will bring the Nuro Driver™ up on new vehicle platforms alongside OEM and supplier engineers, and see your code drive real vehicles on public roads. We&#39;re hiring across levels, from engineers with a couple years of embedded experience to those who&#39;ve shipped a production automotive launch.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Work&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, implement and test embedded C software for safety-critical multicore automotive microcontrollers, spanning base software such as RTOS, device drivers, scheduling and bootloader, middleware such as inter-component messaging and end-to-end protection, and application components such as actuator interface, body controls, power management and fault management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrate the Nuro Driver™ with new vehicle platforms: define and implement CAN and Ethernet interfaces with OEM ECUs, adapt actuator and body-control interfaces, and validate them on bench and in vehicle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take part in hands-on device and vehicle bring-up, prototyping and debugging on multiple vehicle platforms, from first power-on to autonomous driving.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain the team&#39;s verification infrastructure: unit tests, hardware-in-the-loop benches and vehicle test procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work within an ISO 26262 development process: define software requirements from system safety requirements, then implement and verify them with full traceability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate daily with systems, safety, hardware, controls and autonomy engineers, and with OEM and supplier partners, from definition through verification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;B.S. or higher in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, Electrical Engineering or a closely related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of industry experience developing embedded software in C, including work on a real-time operating system.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid computer science fundamentals: data structures, concurrency and algorithm design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of microcontroller internals and peripherals, with depth in at least one of device driver development, CAN or automotive Ethernet, bootloaders and software update, embedded security, or vehicle-level integration and test.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong problem-solving and debugging skills, clear written and spoken communication, and a track record of working well with engineers from other disciplines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable at the bench with debug probes, oscilloscopes, logic analyzers and CAN tools. You enjoy finding out why hardware and software disagree.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Points&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of embedded development in the automotive or autonomous vehicle industry, including a production launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on functional safety experience with ISO 26262, or safety-critical development in another regulated industry such as DO-178C or IEC 62304.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Infineon AURIX TC3xx, SafeRTOS or FreeRTOS, or AUTOSAR Classic base software such as MCAL and communication stacks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Vehicle network integration experience: DBC and ARXML, UDS diagnostics, E2E protection, time synchronization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of vehicle functions, vehicle dynamics or control theory.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Nuro, your base pay is one part of your total compensation package. For this position, the reasonably expected base pay range is between $176,400 and $264,000 for the level at which this job has been scoped. Your base pay will depend on several factors, including your experience, qualifications, education, location, and skills. In the event that you are considered for a different level, a higher or lower pay range would apply. This position is also eligible for an annual performance bonus, equity, and a competitive benefits package.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At Nuro, we celebrate differences and are committed to a diverse workplace that fosters inclusion and psychological safety for all employees. Nuro is proud to be an equal opportunity employer and expressly prohibits any form of workplace discrimination based on race, color, religion, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, age, genetic information, disability, veteran status, or any other legally protected characteristics. #LI-DNP&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;","departments":[{"id":247413,"name":"Controls, Pose and ESWE","child_ids":[],"parent_id":247412}],"offices":[{"id":23484,"name":"California - HQ","location":"Nuro HQ - Mountain View, CA","child_ids":[],"parent_id":83166}],"ai_disclaimer":null,"include_ai_disclaimer":false,"ai_opt_out_request_url":"http://app.greenhouse.io/ai_opt_out_request/job_post/8263454/ai_opt_out"},{"absolute_url":"https://nuro.ai/careersitem?gh_jid=8114353","data_compliance":[{"type":"gdpr","requires_consent":false,"requires_processing_consent":false,"requires_retention_consent":false,"retention_period":null,"demographic_data_consent_applies":false}],"internal_job_id":3514779,"location":{"name":"Mountain View, California (HQ)"},"metadata":[{"id":53829309,"name":"Location","value":"California - HQ","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":4977510,"name":"Department","value":"Finance","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":954897,"name":"Job Family","value":"Financial Reporting","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":4993730,"name":"Time Type","value":"Full-time","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":4978502,"name":"Worker Sub-Type","value":"Regular","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":6653805,"name":"Department (Job Board)","value":"Finance","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":6644840,"name":"Org (Job Board)","value":"Finance","value_type":"single_select"}],"id":8114353,"updated_at":"2026-10-22T14:10:02-04:00","requisition_id":"R-103002","title":"Senior Manager, FP&A","company_name":"Nuro","first_published":"2026-08-18T00:52:00-04:00","language":"en","application_deadline":null,"content":"&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nuro believes self-driving vehicles are the most immediate and profound opportunity for AI to drive positive change in the physical world. Safer streets, more time for what matters, and easier access to the world around us, that’s why we’re building a universal autonomy platform: self-driving for all roads and all rides.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded in 2016, Nuro is a physical AI company developing Level 4 autonomous driving technology for a wide range of vehicles, use cases, and markets. Powered by the Nuro Driver™, our universal autonomy platform enables the global mobility ecosystem to deploy autonomy at scale, from robotaxis and logistics fleets to personal vehicles.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With years of real-world deployment experience and a flexible, partner-led business model, Nuro is working toward a future where millions of autonomous vehicles powered by our technology help make everyday life safer, easier, and more connected.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nuro has raised over $2B in capital from Uber, NVIDIA, Google, Softbank, Fidelity, T. Rowe Price, and other leading investors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nuro’s Finance team is small and deeply embedded in the business. We partner directly with engineering, operations, and G&amp;amp;A leaders on how capital gets allocated, and we support the company’s most consequential decisions, from partnership economics to long-range planning. As Nuro expands its commercial partnerships, we are building a dedicated Corporate FP&amp;amp;A function. This role will be the first hire and foundational owner of that function. You will have significant autonomy, broad visibility, and direct access to senior leadership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Senior Manager, Corporate FP&amp;amp;A, you will establish and own Nuro’s company-wide financial planning and reporting infrastructure. You will lead the company-wide budget, headcount plan, monthly consolidated budget-versus-actuals, and rolling reforecast, which together guide how the executive team manages the business. You will also build the systems, data model, and governance processes that support those activities. Nuro’s planning process is spreadsheet-based today, so you are not inheriting a machine to maintain; you are building one. You will report to the Head of Finance and take your work directly to our CFO and co-CEOs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Work&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the financial operating rhythm. &lt;/strong&gt;You will build and run the annual budget and headcount plan end to end: timeline, data requirements, templates, executive alignment, approvals, and communication. From there you will own the monthly consolidated budget-versus-actuals and a rolling reforecast process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the headcount plan. &lt;/strong&gt;You will own the company headcount plan of record and the incremental headcount approval process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Executive and board reporting. &lt;/strong&gt;You will produce the financial reporting our executive team and board rely on, spanning working-team detail to board-level narrative. Your job is not to publish variances; it is to say what changed, why it changed, what it means, and what we should do about it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accounting partnership and cash-to-GAAP fluency. &lt;/strong&gt;You will work hand in hand with Accounting to connect FP&amp;amp;A to the close, the chart of accounts, and the ERP, so plan and actuals reconcile. You will build the ability to flex between accrual and cash views of key metrics, and help leadership understand which view is the right one for a given decision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Spend governance. &lt;/strong&gt;You will design and run the processes that control how Nuro commits capital: incremental headcount approvals and budget adjustment proposals. You will make these processes rigorous enough to trust and fast enough to adapt to the pace of our business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scenario modeling. &lt;/strong&gt;Working closely with our Strategic Finance team, you will model the cash and accounting impacts of major partnerships, program launches, and financing events, and stress-test the plan against a range of outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Financial systems and data. &lt;/strong&gt;You will own FP&amp;amp;A systems and data. You will select and implement a planning platform and build the foundation underneath it, including hierarchies, cost drivers, and dimensionality, so that we can plan and report at speed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI adoption. &lt;/strong&gt;You will actively track and adopt AI tooling to make FP&amp;amp;A faster, more flexible, and more accurate. We expect this function to be a proving ground for what a modern, AI-native finance team looks like, and we will give you room to build it that way.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;7+ years of finance experience, including 3+ years in FP&amp;amp;A at a scaled technology company. &lt;/strong&gt;You have personally owned a planning cycle and seen what works and doesn’t.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You have operated at a public-company standard. &lt;/strong&gt;You have worked inside a publicly traded technology company, or you have helped take a company through IPO readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GAAP fluency across all three financial statements. &lt;/strong&gt;You understand cash-flow dynamics and can move confidently between cash and GAAP views of the business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hands-on experience with planning systems. &lt;/strong&gt;You’ve worked on a planning platform such as Anaplan, Workday Adaptive Planning, or Oracle Hyperion, and understand how it integrates with an ERP. You have opinions about what to build in the tool and what to leave out of it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You can drive a company-wide process. &lt;/strong&gt;You set timelines and objectives, obtain approvals, build buy-in across functions, communicate clearly, hold teams accountable, check the work, chase the follow-ups, and land the output.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You see the big picture and the details. &lt;/strong&gt;Variances tie, and you can tell leadership what in the P&amp;amp;L actually matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;One team. &lt;/strong&gt;Our Finance team is lean and priorities move quickly. You will collaborate closely with the rest of Strategic Finance to get done whatever is most important, rather than defending a lane.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Points&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ve built or managed a high-performance FP&amp;amp;A team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ve led the implementation of planning software&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have been through an IPO, or been directly involved in IPO preparation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in AI, hardware, automotive, or other hard-tech businesses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have owned a company headcount plan end-to-end in partnership with a People or Talent organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Nuro, your base pay is one part of your total compensation package. For this position, the reasonably expected base pay range is between $176,400 and $264,600 for the level at which this job has been scoped. Your base pay will depend on several factors, including your experience, qualifications, education, location, and skills. In the event that you are considered for a different level, a higher or lower pay range would apply. This position is also eligible for an annual performance bonus, equity, and a competitive benefits package.&lt;/p&gt;
