,"first_published":"2026-10-02T15:50:00-04:00","language":"en","application_deadline":null,"content":"&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nuro believes self-driving vehicles are the most immediate and profound opportunity for AI to drive positive change in the physical world. Safer streets, more time for what matters, and easier access to the world around us, that’s why we’re building a universal autonomy platform: self-driving for all roads and all rides.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Founded in 2016, Nuro is a physical AI company developing Level 4 autonomous driving technology for a wide range of vehicles, use cases, and markets. Powered by the Nuro Driver™, our universal autonomy platform enables the global mobility ecosystem to deploy autonomy at scale, from robotaxis and logistics fleets to personal vehicles.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;With years of real-world deployment experience and a flexible, partner-led business model, Nuro is working toward a future where millions of autonomous vehicles powered by our technology help make everyday life safer, easier, and more connected.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Nuro has raised over $2B in capital from Uber, NVIDIA, Google, Softbank, Fidelity, T. Rowe Price, and other leading investors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Senior Program Manager, Compliance Reporting will be part of the Commercialization &amp;amp; Evaluation team within Software Operations. In this role, you will lead the planning and execution of regulatory reporting programs that support the company’s legal, compliance, and operational obligations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work cross-functionally with Public Trust, Data Platform, Safety, and Software Operations teams to translate complex requirements into clear plans, reliable reporting processes, and actionable operational practices. You will also implement and continuously improve operational and review processes as needed to ensure reporting deliverables are accurate, complete, timely, and supported by thorough documentation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role requires strong program management, exceptional attention to detail, and the ability to operate independently in a fast-paced, highly regulated environment. You will be responsible for driving work from requirements gathering through submission and follow-up, while communicating clearly with technical, legal, and executive stakeholders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Work&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own end-to-end program management for regulatory reporting deliverables, from requirements gathering through submission and follow-up.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage tight, often externally imposed timelines across multiple regulatory reporting work streams simultaneously.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Public Trust and Legal teams to ensure reporting accurately reflects current legal and compliance obligations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Software Operations teams to gather data, verify accuracy, and ensure operational readiness for reporting requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, implement, and improve operational, documentation, and review processes that support consistent and high-quality reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review and interpret legal and regulatory documents, translating obligations into clear, actionable program plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish appropriate review mechanisms, approval workflows, and quality controls for reporting materials.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Draft, edit, and proofread reporting materials and internal communications with a high degree of accuracy and clarity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify risks to reporting timelines or quality early and independently drive mitigation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain thorough documentation and audit trails to support regulatory inquiries, audits, or reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate program status, risks, decisions, and outcomes clearly to stakeholders across technical, legal, and executive audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of program management experience, ideally in a regulated, compliance-heavy, or public-sector-adjacent environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to produce clear, precise, and error-free materials under deadline pressure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong attention to detail, particularly when working with legal, regulatory, or compliance documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to manage multiple competing priorities and tight timelines independently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with or alongside Public Trust, regulatory, legal, or compliance teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort working closely with software operations teams and translating technical processes into reporting requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High degree of self-direction; able to operate effectively with minimal oversight.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Points&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience working directly with regulators or with legal documents, regulatory filings, or contract language.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in the autonomous vehicle industry or another highly regulated technology sector.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Public Trust or government relations processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting audits, regulatory reviews, or formal compliance inquiries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building scalable reporting, documentation, or review programs in a growing organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At Nuro, your base pay is one part of your total compensation package. For this position, the reasonably expected base pay range is between $132,300.00 and $198,450.00 for the level at which this job has been scoped. Your base pay will depend on several factors, including your experience, qualifications, education, location, and skills. In the event that you are considered for a different level, a higher or lower pay range would apply. This position is also eligible for an annual performance bonus, equity, and a competitive benefits package.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At Nuro, we celebrate differences and are committed to a diverse workplace that fosters inclusion and psychological safety for all employees. Nuro is proud to be an equal opportunity employer and expressly prohibits any form of workplace discrimination based on race, color, religion, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, age, genetic information, disability, veteran status, or any other legally protected characteristics. #LI-CD1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;","departments":[{"id":293798,"name":"Software Operations","child_ids":[],"parent_id":247414}],"offices":[{"id":23484,"name":"California - HQ","location":"Nuro HQ - Mountain View, CA","child_ids":[],"parent_id":83166}],"ai_disclaimer":null,"include_ai_disclaimer":false,"ai_opt_out_request_url":"http://app.greenhouse.io/ai_opt_out_request/job_post/8249825/ai_opt_out"},{"absolute_url":"https://nuro.ai/careersitem?gh_jid=8180896","data_compliance":[{"type":"gdpr","requires_consent":false,"requires_processing_consent":false,"requires_retention_consent":false,"retention_period":null,"demographic_data_consent_applies":false}],"internal_job_id":3540129,"location":{"name":"Mountain View, California (HQ)"},"metadata":[{"id":53829309,"name":"Location","value":"California - HQ","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":4977510,"name":"Department","value":"Software Operations","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":954897,"name":"Job Family","value":"Software Operations","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":4993730,"name":"Time Type","value":"Full-time","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":4978502,"name":"Worker Sub-Type","value":"Regular","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":6653805,"name":"Department (Job Board)","value":"Software Operations","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":6644840,"name":"Org (Job Board)","value":"Software","value_type":"single_select"}],"id":8180896,"updated_at":"2026-10-09T11:02:43-04:00","requisition_id":"R-103098","title":"Senior Program Manager, Perception Data Operations","company_name":"Nuro","first_published":"2026-09-04T18:44:56-04:00","language":"en","application_deadline":null,"content":"&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nuro believes self-driving vehicles are the most immediate and profound opportunity for AI to drive positive change in the physical world. Safer streets, more time for what matters, and easier access to the world around us, that’s why we’re building a universal autonomy platform: self-driving for all roads and all rides.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Founded in 2016, Nuro is a physical AI company developing Level 4 autonomous driving technology for a wide range of vehicles, use cases, and markets. Powered by the Nuro Driver™, our universal autonomy platform enables the global mobility ecosystem to deploy autonomy at scale, from robotaxis and logistics fleets to personal vehicles.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;With years of real-world deployment experience and a flexible, partner-led business model, Nuro is working toward a future where millions of autonomous vehicles powered by our technology help make everyday life safer, easier, and more connected.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Nuro has raised over $2B in capital from Uber, NVIDIA, Google, Softbank, Fidelity, T. Rowe Price, and other leading investors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Perception ML Operations team sits at the center of how Nuro&#39;s vehicles learn to see. We are responsible for the training and evaluation data that powers perception models across every sensor modality: vision, lidar, radar, and beyond. We work alongside ML engineers, product owners, data engineers, and external labeling partners to turn ambiguous, fast-moving requirements into data deliverables the Perception team can build on with confidence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a team that operates at the intersection of ML urgency and operational discipline. Here is what the work actually looks like day-to-day:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sitting in a roadmap review, hearing a new feature requirement land, and walking out with a concrete data collection and labeling plan already scoped against timeline and budget.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reviewing vendor throughput against milestone dates and catching a capacity gap before it would become a release risk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Querying pipeline data directly to understand where quality is slipping, rather than waiting for a ticket or ML engineer to surface the problem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Being the person Perception Engineering calls when they need to know whether a data deliverable is real, on time, and within budget, and making sure the team you manage translates that bar into terms vendors can execute against without ambiguity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If that sounds like the kind of ownership that energizes you, we would love to talk.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a role built for someone who wants to own outcomes, not just track them. You will translate company-wide perception feature requirements into concrete data deliverables, manage vendor allocation and budget against Nuro&#39;s milestone and release timelines, and keep a clear, defensible view of outcomes, risk, and data quality across the pipelines you own — distinguishing a one-off labeling error from a systemic labeling process problem, and closing the gap either way.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The work connects directly to Nuro&#39;s mission. Perception models are only as good as the data behind them, and every gap in coverage, every misallocated vendor hour, and every quality blind spot eventually shows up in how the vehicle sees the world. You are the person who catches that upstream, before it becomes an engineering fire drill or a safety question.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll partner closely with ML engineering leadership, product owners, and vendor operations, with the access and visibility to make real calls on scope, budget, and quality tradeoffs. What we ask in return is rigor, clear communication, and genuine ownership of the outcome.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Work&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Translate Requirements into Deliverables&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Synthesize company-wide perception feature needs into detailed, actionable data deliverables covering vision, LiDAR, and additional sensor modalities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the end-to-end labeling process, from data availability through an outcome Perception can train on, directing data annotation partners to execute against that bar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own Vendor Allocation and Budget&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage vendor allocation and budgeting in direct alignment with Nuro&#39;s milestone and release timelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee large-scale vendor and managed service provider relationships against quality, latency, and volume targets, and hold them accountable when performance drifts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Track Outcomes, Risk, and Quality&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and maintain clear, current tracking of outcomes, risk, and data quality so that status is never a surprise to engineering or leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own quality as an outcome, not just a status: define what &quot;good&quot; looks like for deliverables within your pipelines, and hold vendors to that bar before problems surface downstream.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In response to quality dips, identify whether the issue is an isolated labeling error or a broader process failure, and address the root cause rather than just the single error.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate high-level product roadmaps and engineering requirements into granular operational execution plans, with resource allocation and throughput modeled explicitly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Query databases directly using SQL (Python a plus) to analyze throughput and quality metrics and generate reporting without waiting on engineering support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are not looking for someone who has done everything. We are looking for someone who thinks in systems, owns outcomes rather than status updates, and has genuine command of both the operational and technical sides of perception data.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in Technical Program Management or Operations Strategy, managing complex, cross-functional programs within technology, autonomous driving, or AI/ML.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to translate high-level product roadmaps and engineering requirements into granular operational execution plans, including managing resource allocation and throughput for large-scale workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience overseeing large-scale vendor operations or managed service providers, specifically against quality, latency, and volume targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with SQL to query databases, analyze throughput metrics, and generate reports independently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of holding vendors accountable to a quality bar you&#39;ve defined yourself, not just monitoring metrics someone else set.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Points&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in autonomous vehicles, robotics, computer vision, or ML model training.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience in ML engineering, data engineering, or technical consulting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated track record of improving data quality or throughput at scale, with metrics to show for it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with autonomous vehicle sensor modalities (LiDAR, Radar, Camera, Thermal) and their respective data annotation requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in a technical or business discipline, or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Nuro, your base pay is one part of your total compensation package. For this position, the reasonably expected base pay range is between $132,000 and $198,000 for the level at which this job has been scoped. Your base pay will depend on several factors, including your experience, qualifications, education, location, and skills. In the event that you are considered for a different level, a higher or lower pay range would apply. This position is also eligible for an annual performance bonus, equity, and a competitive benefits package.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At Nuro, we celebrate differences and are committed to a diverse workplace that fosters inclusion and psychological safety for all employees. Nuro is proud to be an equal opportunity employer and expressly prohibits any form of workplace discrimination based on race, color, religion, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, age, genetic information, disability, veteran status, or any other legally protected characteristics. #LI-DNP&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;","departments":[{"id":293798,"name":"Software Operations","child_ids":[],"parent_id":247414}],"offices":[{"id":23484,"name":"California - HQ","location":"Nuro HQ - Mountain View, CA","child_ids":[],"parent_id":83166}],"ai_disclaimer":null,"include_ai_disclaimer":false,"ai_opt_out_request_url":"http://app.greenhouse.io/ai_opt_out_request/job_post/8180896/ai_opt_out"},{"absolute_url":"https://nuro.ai/careersitem?gh_jid=7838576","data_compliance":[{"type":"gdpr","requires_consent":false,"requires_processing_consent":false,"requires_retention_consent":false,"retention_period":null,"demographic_data_consent_applies":false}],"internal_job_id":3418314,"location":{"name":"Mountain View, California (HQ)"},"metadata":[{"id":53829309,"name":"Location","value":"California - HQ","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":4977510,"name":"Department","value":"Software Operations","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":954897,"name":"Job Family","value":"Software Operations","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":4993730,"name":"Time Type","value":"Full-time","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":4978502,"name":"Worker Sub-Type","value":"Regular","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":6653805,"name":"Department (Job Board)","value":"Software Operations","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":6644840,"name":"Org (Job Board)","value":"Software","value_type":"single_select"}],"id":7838576,"updated_at":"2026-10-09T11:02:43-04:00","requisition_id":"R-102722","title":"Senior Program Manager, Validation Operations","company_name":"Nuro","first_published":"2026-05-11T21:06:20-04:00","language":"en","application_deadline":null,"content":"&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nuro believes self-driving vehicles are the most immediate and profound opportunity for AI to drive positive change in the physical world. Safer streets, more time for what matters, and easier access to the world around us, that’s why we’re building a universal autonomy platform: self-driving for all roads and all rides.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Founded in 2016, Nuro is a physical AI company developing Level 4 autonomous driving technology for a wide range of vehicles, use cases, and markets. Powered by the Nuro Driver™, our universal autonomy platform enables the global mobility ecosystem to deploy autonomy at scale, from robotaxis and logistics fleets to personal vehicles.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;With years of real-world deployment experience and a flexible, partner-led business model, Nuro is working toward a future where millions of autonomous vehicles powered by our technology help make everyday life safer, easier, and more connected.&amp;nbsp;Nuro has raised over $2B in capital from Uber, NVIDIA, Google, Softbank, Fidelity, T. Rowe Price, and other leading investors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Software Operations is the processing muscle behind Nuro Driver. We take the onroad miles our fleet collects and turn them into usable data, which becomes the foundation everything downstream depends on. Within Software Operations, Validation Operations holds the bar for safety and system testing, making sure our autonomous driving software is safe before it ever hits the road. It&#39;s careful, consequential work, and we take it seriously.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;About the Role&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Own the systems that make validation operations accurate, scalable, and ready for Nuro’s next stage of growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Program Manager on the Software Operations team, you’ll partner with Autonomy, Systems, and Data Platform Engineering to deliver the high-quality data that powers critical validation and expansion efforts. You’ll serve as the bridge between Engineering, Operations, and our offshore partner, upholding the quality bar, building scalable workflows, and driving performance across the ecosystem.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a high-ownership role for someone who thrives in ambiguity and wants to make a measurable impact. You’ll investigate failures at their root, turn data into decisions, and lead the changes that keep quality, delivery, and operational confidence high.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;About the Work&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll lead the day-to-day operations that keep validation data flowing, accurate, and on schedule, bringing structure to ambiguity and turning quality gaps into lasting improvements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Support critical validation programs:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner with Autonomy, Systems, and Data Platform Engineering to deliver the operational support and data that validation and expansion efforts depend on.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Set the quality standard&lt;/strong&gt;: Define metrics, sampling approaches, workflows, and operating mechanisms that enable consistent, scalable data quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Diagnose and fix what’s broken:&lt;/strong&gt; Audit live workflows, query databases, and trace accuracy or pipeline failures to their root cause, then drive measurable corrective action.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead global operations&lt;/strong&gt;: Own the offshore vendor relationship, including budget, capacity, performance, and quality outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive improvement: &lt;/strong&gt;Lead adoption of improved operational practices through clear documentation, stakeholder engagement, pilot programs, and change management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build the team:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;Lead a small in-house team, strengthen oversight, and create processes that evolve with Nuro’s needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Align teams around action&lt;/strong&gt;: Translate complex operational and technical issues into clear recommendations for Engineering, Operations, and leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You won’t just manage validation operations. You’ll make the whole function better, more scalable, and more trusted.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of program management experience embedded with software validation and/or AI/ML operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Quality-obsessed approach to program management: energized by finding what is broken, not just by shipping on time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep familiarity with data pipelines and labeling ecosystems, including annotation workflows, quality sampling, taxonomy design, and inter-annotator agreement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of identifying and closing data quality gaps, with measurable impact on accuracy or model performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing large-scale offshore or globally distributed annotation teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency querying data with SQL and BigQuery, and using KPIs to drive prioritization, capacity management, and continuous improvement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work both strategically and hands-on, from designing a quality framework to personally tracing a labeling fault through a database&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High agency and a history of building processes where none exist&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear written and verbal communication, with the ability to influence and make complex information accessible to technical and non-technical audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in a technical or business discipline, or equivalent practical experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Points&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in autonomous vehicles, software validation, robotics or data engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Nuro, your base pay is one part of your total compensation package. For this position, the reasonably expected base pay range is between $132,000 and $198,000 for the level at which this job has been scoped. Your base pay will depend on several factors, including your experience, qualifications, education, location, and skills. In the event that you are considered for a different level, a higher or lower pay range would apply. This position is also eligible for an annual performance bonus, equity, and a competitive benefits package.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At Nuro, we celebrate differences and are committed to a diverse workplace that fosters inclusion and psychological safety for all employees. Nuro is proud to be an equal opportunity employer and expressly prohibits any form of workplace discrimination based on race, color, religion, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, age, genetic information, disability, veteran status, or any other legally protected characteristics. #LI-CD1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;","departments":[{"id":293798,"name":"Software Operations","child_ids":[],"parent_id":247414}],"offices":[{"id":23484,"name":"California - HQ","location":"Nuro HQ - Mountain View, CA","child_ids":[],"parent_id":83166}],"ai_disclaimer":null,"include_ai_disclaimer":false,"ai_opt_out_request_url":"http://app.greenhouse.io/ai_opt_out_request/job_post/7838576/ai_opt_out"},{"absolute_url":"https://nuro.ai/careersitem?gh_jid=8275504","data_compliance":[{"type":"gdpr","requires_consent":false,"requires_processing_consent":false,"requires_retention_consent":false,"retention_period":null,"demographic_data_consent_applies":false}],"internal_job_id":3580402,"location":{"name":"Mountain View, California (HQ)"},"metadata":[{"id":53829309,"name":"Location","value":"California - HQ","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":4977510,"name":"Department","value":"Sensors Engineering","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":954897,"name":"Job Family","value":"Embedded Software Engineering","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":4993730,"name":"Time Type","value":"Full-time","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":4978502,"name":"Worker Sub-Type","value":"Regular","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":6653805,"name":"Department (Job Board)","value":"AV Hardware Engineering","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":6644840,"name":"Org (Job Board)","value":"Hardware & Manufacturing","value_type":"single_select"}],"id":8275504,"updated_at":"2026-10-13T17:09:33-04:00","requisition_id":"R-103182","title":"Senior Radar Systems Engineer","company_name":"Nuro","first_published":"2026-10-13T17:09:33-04:00","language":"en","application_deadline":null,"content":"&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nuro believes self-driving vehicles are the most immediate and profound opportunity for AI to drive positive change in the physical world. Safer streets, more time for what matters, and easier access to the world around us, that’s why we’re building a universal autonomy platform: self-driving for all roads and all rides.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Founded in 2016, Nuro is a physical AI company developing Level 4 autonomous driving technology for a wide range of vehicles, use cases, and markets. Powered by the Nuro Driver™, our universal autonomy platform enables the global mobility ecosystem to deploy autonomy at scale, from robotaxis and logistics fleets to personal vehicles.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;With years of real-world deployment experience and a flexible, partner-led business model, Nuro is working toward a future where millions of autonomous vehicles powered by our technology help make everyday life safer, easier, and more connected.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Nuro has raised over $2B in capital from Uber, NVIDIA, Google, Softbank, Fidelity, T. Rowe Price, and other leading investors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Our Sensors Engineering Team is the backbone of our self-driving system&#39;s perception, responsible for selecting, developing, testing and integrating the full suite of sensors that power our autonomous vehicles. This critical group has end-to-end ownership of the hardware, drivers, and system-level integration for core sensors like cameras, lidar and radar, as well as ancillary components such as Inertial Measurement Units and microphones. We are a highly collaborative, multidisciplinary team that works in lockstep with our Software Infrastructure, Mechanical Design, and Supplier Management partners to ensure our vehicles perceive the world accurately, reliably, and safely&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a Senior Radar System Engineer to guide the technical strategy, evaluation, and supplier development of Nuro’s radar sensing capability. You’ll set technical direction, raise the bar on how we evaluate and select sensors, and mentor the engineers working alongside you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a deep, hands-on role for someone who has designed radar systems and understands them end to end, from antennas and MMICs to DSP and the supply chain behind them. Your expertise will shape how Nuro defines excellence in radar. You’ll set the standard for our hardware, evaluate the best sensors in the market against it, and work with suppliers to build the capabilities our autonomous driving system needs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Influence suppliers:&lt;/strong&gt; Work directly with vendors on component level decisions and with Tier 1 module suppliers on system-level performance, cost, and reliability. You’ll build long lasting partnerships with key players.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Balance cost and performance:&lt;/strong&gt; Make trade offs between price, manufacturability, and performance so our sensor choices are technically excellent and commercially viable at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Connect teams:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner with Perception, Systems, and Product to turn their needs into clear sensor requirements, and bring supply base insights to leadership to build an actionable roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Work&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the technical direction for our Radar evaluation and selection strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define Radar performance requirements, specifications, and evaluation criteria, grounded in real downstream perception and system needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, run, and standardize rigorous bench and in-context evaluation methodologies for candidate Radar sensors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive supplier engagements at both Tier 1 and Tier 2 levels, influencing component roadmaps and full-module designs to align with our requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead technical due diligence on Radar vendors and technologies, producing clear comparative assessments and recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor and grow the existing Radar team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Perception, Software, and Mechanical teams to ensure Radar selections integrate cleanly into the broader sensing and compute architecture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain strong, long-term partnerships across the Radar supply base, joint development programs, and relevant industry/standards bodies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate technical roadmaps, trade-offs, and recommendations clearly to engineering peers and executive stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;B.S., M.S., or Ph.D. in Electrical Engineering,Telecommunication, Physics, Computer Engineering, or a related technical field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of professional engineering experience, with substantial hands-on work on Radar or closely adjacent sensing systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep, demonstrable expertise in Radar fundamentals: link budget, antenna technologies, signal processing (FFT, CFAR, detection) and design tradeoffs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to balance price and performance, making sound engineering and commercial trade-offs around cost, manufacturability, and capability to land on the right solution at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of evaluating, specifying, and selecting sensor hardware, with a structured, data-driven approach to benchmarking and qualification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience influencing suppliers at the component (Tier 2) and module/system (Tier 1) level, including driving technical requirements from evaluation through production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comprehensive understanding of the automotive Radar ecosystem, vendors, technology landscape, cost and manufacturability drivers, and emerging trends.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience mentoring engineers and elevating the technical capability of those around you.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with automotive or other safety-critical product cycles, including validation, reliability, and functional safety standards (e.g., ISO 26262), is strongly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and presentation skills, with the ability to articulate complex technical trade-offs clearly to both expert and executive audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A collaborative, partnership-oriented approach and the credibility to build trust with internal teams and external suppliers alike.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Nuro, your base pay is one part of your total compensation package. For this position, the reasonably expected base pay range is between $193,930 and $291,150 for the level at which this job has been scoped. Your base pay will depend on several factors, including your experience, qualifications, education, location, and skills. In the event that you are considered for a different level, a higher or lower pay range would apply. This position is also eligible for an annual performance bonus, equity, and a competitive benefits package.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At Nuro, we celebrate differences and are committed to a diverse workplace that fosters inclusion and psychological safety for all employees. Nuro is proud to be an equal opportunity employer and expressly prohibits any form of workplace discrimination based on race, color, religion, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, age, genetic information, disability, veteran status, or any other legally protected characteristics. #LI-DNP&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;","departments":[{"id":87105,"name":"Sensors Engineering","child_ids":[],"parent_id":247411}],"offices":[],"ai_disclaimer":null,"include_ai_disclaimer":false,"ai_opt_out_request_url":"http://app.greenhouse.io/ai_opt_out_request/job_post/8275504/ai_opt_out"},{"absolute_url":"https://nuro.ai/careersitem?gh_jid=8279156","data_compliance":[{"type":"gdpr","requires_consent":false,"requires_processing_consent":false,"requires_retention_consent":false,"retention_period":null,"demographic_data_consent_applies":false}],"internal_job_id":3539993,"location":{"name":"Mountain View, California (HQ)"},"metadata":[{"id":53829309,"name":"Location","value":"California - HQ","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":4977510,"name":"Department","value":"Technical Program Management, AI Platform","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":954897,"name":"Job Family","value":"Technical Project Management","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":4993730,"name":"Time Type","value":"Full-time","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":4978502,"name":"Worker Sub-Type","value":"Regular","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":6653805,"name":"Department (Job Board)","value":"Software TPM","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":6644840,"name":"Org (Job Board)","value":"Technical Program Management","value_type":"single_select"}],"id":8279156,"updated_at":"2026-10-13T13:40:52-04:00","requisition_id":"R-103039","title":"Senior Senior Technical Program Manager, Driverless Readiness & AI Platform Reliability","company_name":"Nuro","first_published":"2026-10-13T13:40:52-04:00","language":"en","application_deadline":null,"content":"&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nuro believes self-driving vehicles are the most immediate and profound opportunity for AI to drive positive change in the physical world. Safer streets, more time for what matters, and easier access to the world around us, that’s why we’re building a universal autonomy platform: self-driving for all roads and all rides.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Founded in 2016, Nuro is a physical AI company developing Level 4 autonomous driving technology for a wide range of vehicles, use cases, and markets. Powered by the Nuro Driver™, our universal autonomy platform enables the global mobility ecosystem to deploy autonomy at scale, from robotaxis and logistics fleets to personal vehicles.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;With years of real-world deployment experience and a flexible, partner-led business model, Nuro is working toward a future where millions of autonomous vehicles powered by our technology help make everyday life safer, easier, and more connected.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Nuro has raised over $2B in capital from Uber, NVIDIA, Google, Softbank, Fidelity, T. Rowe Price, and other leading investors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Technical Program Manager (TPM)&lt;/strong&gt; to drive cross-functional alignment and execution for &lt;strong&gt;AI Platform &lt;/strong&gt;programs at Nuro. This role sits at the intersection of &lt;strong&gt;Systems Engineering, Platform, Data Science and Autonomy&lt;/strong&gt; teams - focused on delivering scalable and reliable verification &amp;amp; validation (V&amp;amp;V) tools that enable systems readiness for &lt;strong&gt;driverless deployment&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll own the end-to-end lifecycle of systems tooling initiatives: defining requirements, managing priorities, coordinating integration with simulation and autonomy stacks, and ensuring test and validation infrastructure meets the evolving needs of driverless programs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Work&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the reliability metrics that gate driverless readiness and drive them to target.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary interface across AI Platform, Systems, Hardware, and Vehicle Ops, running the operating cadence that keeps reliability work aligned and moving.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain detailed execution plans; track progress, risks, and metrics using internal tools (e.g., JIRA , Confluence, custom dashboards).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive issue triage and burndown to resolution, ensuring clear ownership and accountability across teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate field failure patterns into engineering and tooling priorities for the platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with engineering to focus test and validation capacity on the highest-risk failure modes. Identify testing and validation gaps and improve development workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Ops to improve troubleshooting and intervention workflows, reducing time-to-recovery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain execution plans and provide program updates, decision docs, and risk assessments to leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shorten the loop from field failure to validated fix on the fleet.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in &lt;strong&gt;Computer Science, Electrical Engineering, Robotics, or a related field&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5+ years&lt;/strong&gt; of experience in &lt;strong&gt;technical program management&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;systems engineering&lt;/strong&gt;, or &lt;strong&gt;software development&lt;/strong&gt; in robotics, automotive, or related technology domains.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience leading cross-functional programs involving multiple engineering disciplines (software, hardware, autonomy, or systems).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of &lt;strong&gt;system verification and validation&lt;/strong&gt;, testing frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to manage complex dependencies, drive alignment, and communicate effectively across technical and leadership audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with agile program tools (e.g., Jira) and technical documentation platforms (e.g., Confluence).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Points&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with autonomous systems, vehicle platforms, or robotics simulation environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with data and tooling stacks supporting system V&amp;amp;V (e.g., test harnesses, synthetic data generation, regression testing, scenario replay tools).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical depth in Python, C++, or data tooling pipelines sufficient to engage engineers on design trade-offs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience in driverless readiness, safety case validation, or end-to-end system testing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent organizational and interpersonal skills, able to balance fast-paced execution with structured process discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Nuro, your base pay is one part of your total compensation package. For this position, the reasonably expected base pay range is between $160,360 and $240,540 for the level at which this job has been scoped. Your base pay will depend on several factors, including your experience, qualifications, education, location, and skills. In the event that you are considered for a different level, a higher or lower pay range would apply. This position is also eligible for an annual performance bonus, equity, and a competitive benefits package.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At Nuro, we celebrate differences and are committed to a diverse workplace that fosters inclusion and psychological safety for all employees. Nuro is proud to be an equal opportunity employer and expressly prohibits any form of workplace discrimination based on race, color, religion, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, age, genetic information, disability, veteran status, or any other legally protected characteristics.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;","departments":[{"id":293801,"name":"Technical Program Management, AI Platform","child_ids":[],"parent_id":247414}],"offices":[],"ai_disclaimer":null,"include_ai_disclaimer":false,"ai_opt_out_request_url":"http://app.greenhouse.io/ai_opt_out_request/job_post/8279156/ai_opt_out"},{"absolute_url":"https://nuro.ai/careersitem?gh_jid=8282222","data_compliance":[{"type":"gdpr","requires_consent":false,"requires_processing_consent":false,"requires_retention_consent":false,"retention_period":null,"demographic_data_consent_applies":false}],"internal_job_id":3394148,"location":{"name":"Mountain View, California (HQ)"},"metadata":[{"id":53829309,"name":"Location","value":"California - HQ","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":4977510,"name":"Department","value":"Systems","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":954897,"name":"Job Family","value":"Autonomy","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":4993730,"name":"Time Type","value":"Full-time","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":4978502,"name":"Worker Sub-Type","value":"Regular","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":6653805,"name":"Department (Job Board)","value":"Systems","value_type":"single_select"},{"id":6644840,"name":"Org (Job Board)","value":"Software","value_type":"single_select"}],"id":8282222,"updated_at":"2026-10-14T15:03:58-04:00","requisition_id":"R-102683","title":"Senior Software Engineer, Autonomy Behavior Testing","company_name":"Nuro","first_published":"2026-10-14T15:03:58-04:00","language":"en","application_deadline":null,"content":"&lt;div class=&quot;job__description body&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nuro believes self-driving vehicles are the most immediate and profound opportunity for AI to drive positive change in the physical world. Safer streets, more time for what matters, and easier access to the world around us, that’s why we’re building a universal autonomy platform: self-driving for all roads and all rides.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Founded in 2016, Nuro is a physical AI company developing Level 4 autonomous driving technology for a wide range of vehicles, use cases, and markets. Powered by the Nuro Driver™, our universal autonomy platform enables the global mobility ecosystem to deploy autonomy at scale, from robotaxis and logistics fleets to personal vehicles.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;With years of real-world deployment experience and a flexible, partner-led business model, Nuro is working toward a future where millions of autonomous vehicles powered by our technology help make everyday life safer, easier, and more connected.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Nuro has raised over $2B in capital from Uber, NVIDIA, Google, Softbank, Fidelity, T. Rowe Price, and other leading investors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;The Systems Engineering team is responsible for the requirements, architecture, and validation of autonomous driving capabilities across engineering disciplines. This includes designing performance metrics, evaluation methods, and criteria for success, which the team then drives cross-functional via requirement definition and system validation. Systems Engineering works at the intersection of hardware, software, and robot operations, with a deep understanding of technologies in all three. We are a small, high-impact team that sets the checkpoints for autonomy deployment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Senior Software Engineer, Autonomy Behavior Testing role is responsible for transforming Nuro&#39;s Verification &amp;amp; Validation (V&amp;amp;V) ecosystem. You will focus on the technical implementation, standardization, and automation of V&amp;amp;V processes. This involves creating a unified, automated architecture for validation , designing and managing streamlined triage workflows , and continuously improving the testing pipelines to drive informed, data-driven autonomy development. Your work is key to proving the system&#39;s safety by generating test results that support the Autonomy Safety Case.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Work&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role involves hands-on technical work to design, align, structure, and continuously improve automated test pipelines and workflows:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and implement automated test pipelines and tooling, ensuring easy adoption and minimal friction for Systems engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive standardization across all testing modalities by designing, implementing, and managing unified triage workflows across all workstreams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish a continuous feedback loop to improve V&amp;amp;V processes, specifically by leading root cause analyses and identifying testing gaps with Systems engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn identified system and pipeline gaps into concrete technical requests for partner teams (e.g., Data Platform, Simulation, Infra).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate on and validate implemented solutions with partner teams, providing technical guidance, code review, and documentation to ensure solutions are scalable and meet the needs of Systems engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of technical work experience in a relevant area with 3+ years of experience with testing of autonomous vehicles/robotic systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on software experience with the ability to code in Python or C++ for automation and tooling development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in designing, implementing, and managing large scale simulation or test automation pipelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of systems engineering concepts related to autonomy architecture, particularly how sensing, perception, prediction, and planning modules interact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly collaborative, with strong abilities to think and communicate analytically to drive cross-functional projects and provide technical guidance to partner teams like Simulation and Data Platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Points&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with large scale simulation, or behavior verification, or Fault detection and Response testing for&amp;nbsp; L2+ autonomous systems.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience in defining and implementing triage prioritization strategies and workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with linking test results as evidence to support the Autonomy safety case.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience implementing testing pipelines, validation tooling, and triage workflows for complex projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
